And there's some fun facts about Brenda.
关于Brenda还有一些有趣的事实。

228
00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:42.250
Let's hear them.
说来听听。

229
00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:47.450
Brenda and Mindy Kaling were a writing team before The Office.
Brenda和Mindy Kaling在《办公室》之前是一个编剧搭档。

230
00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:54.170
They wrote and performed in an off-Broadway play called Matt and Ben, which was about
她们创作并出演了一部外百老汇戏剧，叫《Matt and Ben》，讲的是

231
00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:57.090
the friendship of Matt Damon and Ben Affleck.
Matt Damon和Ben Affleck的友谊。

232
00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:58.670
And they played Matt and Ben.
她们分别饰演Matt和Ben。

233
00:09:58.850 --> 00:09:59.230
Yes.
没错。

234
00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.830
Brenda played Matt and Mindy played Ben.
Brenda演Matt，Mindy演Ben。

235
00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:08.570
It was set in 1995 and it tells the story of Matt and Ben before they were stars in their
故事背景设定在1995年，讲述了Matt和Ben在成名之前，

236
00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:11.090
apartment fantasizing about being famous.
在公寓里幻想自己成名的故事。

237
00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.570
It was a huge hit.
那部剧非常成功。

238
00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:15.210
It was a smash critical hit.
那是评论界的大热门。

239
00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:15.810
I would have loved to have seen that.
我真希望能去看那场戏。

240
00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:18.870
I looked up the New York Times review and it was just glowing.
我查了《纽约时报》的评论，评价极高。

241
00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:22.390
And this really put them on the map.
这确实让她们一举成名。

242
00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:25.830
And it's definitely what got Mindy noticed.
这绝对是让Mindy受到关注的原因。

243
00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.830
We haven't even talked about this.
我们还没聊到这个呢。

244
00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:30.710
We haven't even mentioned who's coming on the show today.
我们甚至还没提今天谁要来节目。

245
00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:31.390
I know.
我知道。

246
00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:35.150
I was just about to let it roll off my tongue as if we had announced it.
我刚才正准备脱口而出，就好像我们已经宣布过了一样。

247
00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:35.530
I know.
我知道。

248
00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:36.410
I thought about it too.
我也想到了。

249
00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:37.850
And I was like, wait, we didn't even say.
我当时心想，等等，我们还没说呢。

250
00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:43.470
You guys, we have an amazingly huge, awesome, the guest of all guests is on today.
伙计们，今天我们要迎来一位超级重磅、超赞的嘉宾，绝对是嘉宾中的嘉宾。

251
00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:48.750
Greg Daniels, the creator of the show, is coming on the episode today.
本剧的创作者格雷格·丹尼尔斯今天会来参加这期节目。

252
00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.090
He's going to be here any minute.
他随时都会到。

253
00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:52.730
He is going to sit with us.
他会和我们坐在一起。

254
00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:54.990
We're a little giddy, as you can tell.
如你所见，我们有点兴奋。

255
00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:56.530
We're super giddy.
我们超级兴奋。

256
00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.990
And I believe he went and saw this show.
而且我相信他当时去看了这部剧。

257
00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.470
And that's how he discovered Mindy.
他就是那样发现了明迪。

258
00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.750
Yeah, we'll have to ask him.
没错，我们得问问他。

259
00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:03.170
We'll ask him because he'll be here.
我们会问他的，因为他会来这里。

260
00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:04.350
Because he's going to be here.
因为他马上就要到了。

261
00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:05.450
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

262
00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:09.830
Greg Daniels, showrunner of The Office and writer of this episode, will be joining us.
《办公室》的剧集主管兼本集编剧格雷格·丹尼尔斯将加入我们。

263
00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:10.630
That's hilarious.
太搞笑了。

264
00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:12.410
Why did we not lead with that?
我们为什么没把这个放在开头说？

265
00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:13.910
Talk about burying the lead.
这简直是本末倒置。

266
00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.110
I think we're just so excited.
我想我们只是太激动了。

267
00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:18.650
I know I'm watching the clock because he's going to be here soon.
我知道我一直在看时间，因为他很快就要到了。

268
00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:21.730
So I was like, oh, let's get Fast Facts done because then Greg's going to be here.
所以我当时想，哦，赶紧把“快速事实”做完，因为格雷格马上就要来了。

269
00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:23.610
Oh, just get Fast Facts done.
哦，赶紧把“快速事实”做完吧。

270
00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:24.310
Hey, now.
嘿，别这样。

271
00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:26.130
Hurry up and get your Fast Facts done.
快点把你的“快速事实”做完。

272
00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:27.730
I had a good tip in for your Fast Facts.
我本来有个好点子可以给你的“快速事实”用。

273
00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:28.310
No, I'm kidding.
不，我开玩笑的。

274
00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:28.830
I'm kidding.
我开玩笑的。

275
00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:29.350
All right.
好吧。

276
00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:31.930
Well, let's finish with these Fast Facts so that Greg can get in here.
那么，让我们赶紧结束这些“快速事实”，好让格雷格进来。

277
00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:37.750
Fast Fact number three, we shot on location, guys, on a boat.
“快速事实”第三条，伙计们，我们是在外景拍摄的，在一艘船上。

278
00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:39.170
On a boat.
在一艘船上。

279
00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:40.010
On a boat.
在一艘船上。

280
00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:45.050
This was outside of the Long Beach Harbor, which is about 45 minutes south of Los Angeles.
拍摄地点在长滩港外，距离洛杉矶以南约45分钟路程。

281
00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.270
We shot there for three days.
我们在那里拍了三天。

282
00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:51.150
Now, for two of the days, we filmed while the boat was docked.
其中两天，我们是在船停靠时拍摄的。

283
00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:54.150
And then there was one night when we were moving.
还有一天晚上，船是在航行中的。

284
00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:59.250
Because we were in Long Beach and they put us up at a hotel, I had these grand fantasies
因为我们在长滩，他们把我们安置在一家酒店，我当时还有些美好的幻想，

285
00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:06.090
that we were going to be all hanging out back at the hotel and kind of partying or something.
觉得我们会在酒店聚在一起，开开派对什么的。

286
00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:06.370
I don't know.
我不知道。

287
00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:07.250
I had this idea.
我当时就是这么想的。

288
00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:09.230
Yeah, I'd never really been on location before.
是啊，我以前从没真正出过外景。

289
00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:10.610
We never even saw the hotel.
我们甚至都没怎么见过那家酒店。

290
00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:14.310
Literally, we were on the boat all night and we would go to the hotel and maybe sleep a few hours
真的，我们整晚都在船上，然后去酒店可能也就睡几个小时，

291
00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:15.330
and then we'd go right back.
接着就又回去了。

292
00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.150
I have no memory of the hotel.
我对那家酒店一点印象都没有。

293
00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:22.670
Well, no, but I did bring poker chips thinking that we would hang out at the hotel and play
好吧，不，但我确实带了筹码，以为我们会在酒店聚在一起玩玩扑克，

294
00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:24.130
poker, but it never happened.
但那从来没发生过。

295
00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:29.070
We actually filmed from like late afternoon overnight until the sun came up.
我们实际上是从傍晚一直拍到通宵，直到太阳升起。

296
00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:33.590
Yes, I wrote in my journal that we filmed from 2.30 p.m.
是的，我在日记里写道，我们从下午2点半开始拍摄，

297
00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.510
and usually wrapped around 5 a.m.
通常在凌晨5点左右收工。

298
00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:40.050
And I wrote, I felt the motion of that boat all week the next week.
我还写道，接下来的那一整周，我都能感觉到那艘船在晃动。

299
00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:43.290
I would be in line at the grocery store and realize I was swaying.
我在杂货店排队时，会突然意识到自己在摇晃。

300
00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:44.630
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

301
00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:48.870
It was intense because even when the boat wasn't moving, you're still on water.
当时感觉很强烈，因为即使船不动，你还是在水上。

302
00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:53.330
Well, yeah, even, I actually think it's worse when you're just docked because then it's
嗯，是啊，甚至，我其实觉得停靠的时候更糟糕，因为那时候

303
00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:57.830
like doing this weird like, like, kind of thing.
就像在做这种奇怪的，那种，类似的事情。

304
00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:00.810
And when you're moving, you know, it's better.
而当你移动的时候，你知道，感觉会好一些。

305
00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:06.250
It's like a forward motion, but that kind of rocking against the dock for days on it.
那是一种向前的动力，但那种在码头边晃荡了好几天的感觉。

