00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:47.390
If you go on YouTube and like Jenna Fisher Booze Cruise documentary, it'll pop up.
如果你去YouTube搜索“Jenna Fisher Booze Cruise documentary”，它就会弹出来。

321
00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:48.270
It's amazing.
太棒了。

322
00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:50.230
I interviewed crew members.
我采访了剧组成员。

323
00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:52.050
I asked them what they did.
我问他们都在做什么。

324
00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:56.290
And it's very funny because you see us getting on the boat.
这非常有趣，因为你可以看到我们上船时的样子。

325
00:13:56.450 --> 00:14:00.030
Dave Rogers, our editor, I gave him all the footage and he put together this video.
我们的剪辑师Dave Rogers，我把所有素材都给了他，他剪辑了这个视频。

326
00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.130
You see us all getting on the boat.
你可以看到我们所有人上船。

327
00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:04.470
And we're like, yeah, the Booze Cruise.
我们当时说，耶，酒水游轮。

328
00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:07.510
And then the first night we're like, yeah, Booze Cruise.
然后第一天晚上我们说，耶，酒水游轮。

329
00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:08.670
We're still, we're doing it.
我们还在，我们在坚持。

330
00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:09.090
We're doing it.
我们在坚持。

331
00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:15.110
Like by the third night, no one will speak to me, but you definitely see the progression.
到了第三天晚上，没人理我了，但你绝对能看到这种变化过程。

332
00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:18.390
I watched the whole thing and it just made me smile.
我看了整部片子，它让我会心一笑。

333
00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:21.210
I just, man, it just brought me right back.
我只是，天哪，它直接把我带回了过去。

334
00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:23.130
And we also look 12 years old.
而且我们看起来才12岁。

335
00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:24.050
We do.
确实。

336
00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:29.190
We just look so, I was like, oh man, time has marched on across my face.
我们看起来太，我当时想，天哪，岁月已经在我的脸上留下了痕迹。

337
00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:30.290
Oh no.
噢不。

338
00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:32.830
I was like, wow, we look so young.
我当时想，哇，我们看起来太年轻了。

339
00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:34.490
Well, that's all I've got.
好吧，我就这些要说的了。

340
00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:38.110
Should we go get Greg and bring him in here and break down this episode?
我们要不要去把Greg叫来，让他加入我们一起拆解这一集？

341
00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.790
Yes, because I have a ton of note cards.
好的，因为我有一大堆笔记卡。

342
00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.070
You really do.
你确实有。

343
00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:42.830
I really do.
我真的有。

344
00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:51.130
Angela guys got here early because she had so many note cards that she was like, I came in and I was shocked.
Angela她们来得很早，因为她有太多的笔记卡，我进来的时候都惊呆了。

345
00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.790
I said, what is this?
我说，这是什么？

346
00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:54.190
Here it is though.
不过就是这些了。

347
00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:55.410
All right, well, let's do it.
好吧，那我们开始吧。

348
00:14:55.410 --> 00:15:03.680
Hi, I'm Jessica St. Clair and I'm June Diane Raphael.
嗨，我是Jessica St. Clair，我是June Diane Raphael。

349
00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:09.940
And we are two friends trying to survive the chaos and celebrate the joy that life throws our way.
我们是两个试图在生活中生存并庆祝生活带给我们快乐的朋友。

350
00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:13.200
And we do it every week on our podcast, The Deep Dive.
我们每周都会在我们的播客《The Deep Dive》中这样做。

351
00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:17.660
Sometimes we dig into the deep stuff, like how I communicate with my dead best friend.
有时我们会深入探讨一些深刻的话题，比如我如何与我已故的挚友交流。

352
00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:21.700
And sometimes we give bad advice based off a TikTok I saw.
有时我们也会根据我在TikTok上看到的内容给出一些糟糕的建议。

353
00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:23.780
And we're not going to apologize for that.
而且我们对此绝不道歉。

354
00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:24.860
Absolutely not.
绝对不会。

355
00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:28.440
You'll laugh, you'll cry, you'll hire a psychic medium.
你会笑，你会哭，你还会去请灵媒。

356
00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:29.820
Join us, won't you?
加入我们吧，好吗？

357
00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:33.520
Listen to The Deep Dive wherever you get your podcasts from Lemonada Media.
欢迎在各大播客平台收听由Lemonada Media制作的《The Deep Dive》。

358
00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:42.310
Hey guys, we're back from our break.
嘿大家，我们休假回来了。

359
00:15:42.530 --> 00:15:44.910
And we are sitting here with Greg Daniels.
今天我们请到了格雷格·丹尼尔斯（Greg Daniels）。

360
00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:45.490
Yay!
耶！

361
00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.970
Writer of Booze Cruise, showrunner of The Office.
他是《酒后巡游》（Booze Cruise）的编剧，也是《办公室》（The Office）的剧集运作人。

362
00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:51.550
Greg, thank you so much for coming in.
格雷格，非常感谢你能来。

363
00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:53.110
Well, thank you so much for inviting me.
嗯，非常感谢你们的邀请。

364
00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:54.250
I love your show.
我很喜欢你们的节目。

365
00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:55.550
You guys are so good together.
你们俩配合得真好。

366
00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:57.270
It's so entertaining to hear you.
听你们聊天非常有意思。

367
00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:02.090
And it's so fun for me to hear your voices and your points of view and everything.
能听到你们的声音、观点以及所有的一切，对我来说也很有趣。

368
00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:03.870
Thank you so much, Greg.
太感谢了，格雷格。

369
00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:07.010
If not for you, Greg, we would not be best friends and this show wouldn't exiSt.
格雷格，如果不是因为你，我们可能不会成为最好的朋友，这个节目也不会存在。

370
00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:10.630
Our lives would be completely – I don't even know.
我们的生活会完全——我甚至不知道会怎样。

371
00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:14.230
I can't even put it into words, honestly, because now I'll get emotional.
老实说，我甚至无法用言语来表达，因为我现在又要情绪化了。

372
00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:14.790
Here I go.
我要开始了。

373
00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:15.850
Angela's crying already.
安吉拉已经哭了。

374
00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:17.270
I can't.
我不行了。

375
00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:17.650
Sorry.
抱歉。

376
00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:19.250
It just all kind of hit me.
刚才那种感觉一下子涌上来了。

377
00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:27.650
Do you know how Jim says he'll bet a paycheck that Michael in this episode is going to do the Titanic thing?
你记得吉姆说他敢拿工资打赌，迈克尔在这一集里会模仿《泰坦尼克号》的桥段吗？

378
00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:28.030
Yeah.
记得。

379
00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:30.630
I would have said Angela was going to tear up.
我当时就该说安吉拉会哭的。

380
00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:33.430
And it happened already.
结果已经发生了。

381
00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:34.410
It happened so soon.
发生得太快了。

382
00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:34.830
I know.
我知道。

383
00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:35.510
I'm sorry.
对不起。

384
00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:42.730
I just – it just all – like the wave hit me of just gratitude I have for you, just absolute gratitude in my heart.
我只是——我只是——那种感激之情像海浪一样向我袭来，我对你充满了绝对的感激，发自内心的感激。

385
00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:43.250
Likewise.
彼此彼此。

386
00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:43.830
Yeah, you.
是啊，你也是。

387
00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:46.030
It was a great time for all of us.
那对我们所有人来说都是一段美好的时光。

388
00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:50.610
And if your friendship was the only thing that came out of it, that would be cool.
如果你们的友谊是那段经历中唯一的收获，那也很酷。

389
00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:51.230
Aw.
噢。

390
00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.630
And yet it's not, is it?
但事实并非如此，对吧？

391
00:16:55.010 --> 00:17:01.470
Well, Greg, when we have guests, we always like to start with asking them, how did they end up being on The Office?
格雷格，每当有嘉宾来时，我们都喜欢先问他们，他们是怎么参与到《办公室》这部剧的？

392
00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.650
How did you end up developing The Office for American Television?
你是怎么想到要为美国电视观众开发《办公室》的？

393
00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:13.290
I will go back a little ways because I was kind of already with a career at the time that the show started.
我得稍微回溯一下，因为在剧集开始的时候，我已经有了一定的职业生涯。

394
00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:15.490
You had a very successful career, Greg.
格雷格，你当时已经拥有非常成功的职业生涯了。

395
00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:20.150
I mean, you had done King the – I won't list your IMDb, but you were the real deal.
我是说，你做过《山丘之王》——我不会去列举你的IMDb履历，但你是真正的实力派。

396
00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:20.870
Go ahead.
说吧，没关系。

397
00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:22.510
People don't know it enough.
大家对你的了解还不够多。

398
00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:24.390
You created King of the Hill.
你创作了《山丘之王》。

399
00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:24.830
King of the Hill.
《山丘之王》。

400
00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:25.910
And you were running that show.
而且你当时还是那部剧的运作人。

401
00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:26.570
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

402
00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:29.230
But you had written on Saturday Night Live and –
但你当时在《周六夜现场》写过剧本，还有——

403
00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:29.630
Simpsons.
《辛普森一家》。

404
00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:30.850
The Simpsons forever.
永远的《辛普森一家》。

405
00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:34.930
And oh, my gosh, there's that one song that you wrote on The Simpsons that is just amazing.
天哪，你在《辛普森一家》里写的那首歌简直太棒了。

406
00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:36.170
Anyway, okay, okay.
总之，好吧，好吧。

407
00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:37.070
Who needs a quickie mart?
谁需要便利店？

408
00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:38.890
Yes, who needs – yes, yes.
没错，谁需要——对，对。

409
00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.710
Okay, so you were the real deal.
好吧，所以你是真材实料的。

410
00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:43.090
It was – things were cooking.
当时一切都进展得很顺利。

411
00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:43.910
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

412
00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:45.610
So I was in a good position.
所以我当时处境不错。

413
00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:50.090
You know how they say like you need 10,000 hours to be good at something?
你知道人们常说，要精通某件事需要一万个小时的练习吗？

414
00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:50.550
Yes.
知道。

415
00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:55.530
So I had sort of 10,000 hours on The Simpsons and Saturday Night Live, and then I had another
所以我已经在《辛普森一家》和《周六夜现场》积累了一万个小时，然后又在

416
00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:57.470
like 15,000 hours on King of the Hill.
《乡巴佬希尔一家的幸福生活》里积累了大概一万五千个小时。

417
00:17:57.570 --> 00:17:59.230
So I was like prepared.
所以我算是准备好了。

418
00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:08.450
And what happened was my agent sent me the tape of The Office, and it was pretty unknown
当时的情况是，我的经纪人寄给我《办公室》的录像带，那时候它在这边

419
00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:08.950
over here.
还不太出名。

420
00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:10.710
And it had a pretty boring title.
而且名字听起来挺无聊的。

421
00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:12.670
And I didn't watch it.
所以我没看。

422
00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:14.490
The BBC version.
BBC版的那部。

423
00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:15.610
The BBC version, yes.
BBC版，没错。

424
00:18:15.850 --> 00:18:17.350
And so he called me.
于是他给我打了电话。

425
00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:21.290
It was over Christmas, like two years before our show came out.
那是在圣诞节期间，大概在我们剧开播的两年前。

426
00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:25.230
And he said, all right, I'm going to send this to somebody else if you don't watch it.
他说，好吧，如果你再不看，我就把它寄给别人了。

427
00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:26.670
And I was like, oh, okay, hang on, hang on.
我当时就说，哦，好吧，等等，等等。

428
00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:27.370
I'll watch it tonight.
我今晚就看。

429
00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:31.450
And I put it in around 11, and I stayed up till like 3 in the morning watching it.
我大概11点左右放进去看，结果一直看到凌晨3点。

430
00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:33.070
I thought it was just brilliant.
我觉得它简直太精彩了。

431
00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:38.670
So I called, and I said, I really want to meet these guys.
所以我打电话说，我真的很想见见这些人。

432
00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:46.710
And I had been kind of like a good little student always in my career.
在我的职业生涯中，我一直是个乖学生。

433
00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:49.510
And I always wanted to interact with people who I respected.
我总是想和那些我尊敬的人交流。

434
00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:54.950
And I sold an episode to Seinfeld so I could work with Larry David.
我曾卖给《宋飞正传》一集剧本，就是为了能和拉里·大卫合作。

435
00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:57.830
And that was like a career important move for me.
那对我来说是职业生涯中重要的一步。

436
00:18:57.930 --> 00:19:02.230
And I kind of identified that Ricky Gervais and Stephen Merchant had done something that
我当时就认定，瑞奇·热维斯和斯蒂芬·莫昌特做出的作品，

437
00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:06.530
put them in the top ranks of people working in this profession.
让他们跻身于这个行业顶尖人才的行列。

438
00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:07.810
So I really wanted to meet them.
所以我真的很想见见他们。

439
00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:10.430
And I didn't really think it could be adapted.
而且我当时并不觉得它能被改编。

440
00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:12.330
So I was kind of scamming them.
所以我当时有点在“套路”他们。

441
00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:15.110
I was like, I'm going to go meet you and take this interesting meeting.
我心想，我要去见你们，参加这个有趣的会议。

442
00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.690
Take your knowledge from you.
从你们身上学点东西。

443
00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:17.450
Ask you questions.
问你们一些问题。

444
00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:18.570
Build a relationship.
建立一段关系。

445
00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:20.210
Maybe for something in the future.
也许为了将来能合作点什么。

446
00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:20.770
You never know.
谁知道呢。

447
00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:21.630
What's not going to be this?
反正肯定不是这个项目。

448
00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:26.730
And anyway, so we met over at Ben Silverman's office because he had the rights.
总之，我们在本·西尔弗曼的办公室见了面，因为版权在他手里。

449
00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:33.850
And we got along very well because it turned out that they loved American TV, and specifically
我们相处得非常好，因为事实证明他们很喜欢美国电视节目，尤其是

450
00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:34.590
The Simpsons.
《辛普森一家》。

451
00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:40.210
And specifically, their favorite episode, or Ricky's favorite episode, was Homer Badman,
具体来说，他们最喜欢的一集，或者说是瑞奇最喜欢的一集，是《荷马坏人》，

452
00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:40.910
which I had written.
那一集是我写的。

453
00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:42.650
And so we kind of hit it off.
所以我们算是很投缘。

454
00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:43.270
That's amazing.
那太棒了。

455
