就像那种领巾一样的东西。

761
00:33:23.510 --> 00:33:23.770
Yes.
是的。

762
00:33:23.910 --> 00:33:27.610
And then she very slowly just turns into Mindy Kaling.
然后她非常缓慢地就变成了敏迪·卡灵本人。

763
00:33:27.810 --> 00:33:28.270
Yes.
没错。

764
00:33:28.410 --> 00:33:28.730
Basically.
基本上是这样。

765
00:33:29.110 --> 00:33:31.310
And now her hair has transitioned.
现在她的发型已经完成了过渡。

766
00:33:31.670 --> 00:33:38.730
Well, this is a long campaign that Mindy waged behind the scenes, taking, you know,
嗯，这是敏迪在幕后发起的一场长期运动，你知道，她采取了……

767
00:33:38.870 --> 00:33:42.890
and I know she plotted it, and every step was a victory.
我知道她是精心策划的，每一步都是一次胜利。

768
00:33:42.890 --> 00:33:47.530
And a lot of it would be, we'd kind of do a double take and go, hey, wait, what are you
很多时候，我们都会不由得回头看一眼，然后说，嘿，等等，你穿的是

769
00:33:47.530 --> 00:33:47.830
wearing?
什么？

770
00:33:49.050 --> 00:33:49.910
She's sly.
她很狡猾。

771
00:33:49.990 --> 00:33:51.170
She would have slipped something in.
她会悄悄塞进一些私货。

772
00:33:51.450 --> 00:33:51.910
Yeah.
是啊。

773
00:33:52.050 --> 00:33:55.590
And she kind of hijacked that character and made it into her character.
她就这样劫持了这个角色，把它变成了她自己的角色。

774
00:33:56.050 --> 00:33:59.330
Well, we are enjoying watching the slow evolution of this.
嗯，我们很享受观察这个缓慢的演变过程。

775
00:33:59.330 --> 00:33:59.450
Yes.
是的。

776
00:33:59.450 --> 00:34:00.350
It's been really fun.
这真的很有趣。

777
00:34:00.750 --> 00:34:01.150
Yes.
没错。

778
00:34:01.150 --> 00:34:03.060
I think her hair has now transformed.
我想她的发型现在已经彻底改变了。

779
00:34:03.650 --> 00:34:05.970
We're waiting for her wardrobe to transform.
我们还在等她的服装也发生改变。

780
00:34:05.970 --> 00:34:10.570
And also, we're waiting for the first Beyonce reference, which has not happened yet.
而且，我们还在等第一个碧昂丝的梗，目前还没出现过。

781
00:34:10.890 --> 00:34:14.390
Well, Brenda also, I don't know, this is maybe, is this a fast fact?
嗯，布伦达也是，我不知道，这也许算是一个快问快答吗？

782
00:34:14.590 --> 00:34:15.010
Ooh.
噢。

783
00:34:15.170 --> 00:34:15.590
Fast fact?
快问快答？

784
00:34:15.730 --> 00:34:20.270
I did discuss Brenda in fast facts, but we were going to come to you and ask you for
我在快问快答里讨论过布伦达，但我们本来打算来问问你，听听你

785
00:34:20.270 --> 00:34:21.270
your input about Brenda.
对布伦达的看法。

786
00:34:21.490 --> 00:34:28.510
Well, Brenda was Mindy's writing and performance partner in the play that is how I cast Mindy,
嗯，布伦达是敏迪在剧中的写作和表演搭档，我就是通过那部剧选中的敏迪，

787
00:34:28.510 --> 00:34:34.730
because Mindy wrote this off-Broadway play called Matt and Ben about Matt Damon and Ben
因为敏迪写了一部名为《马特与本》的外百老汇剧，讲的是马特·达蒙和本·

788
00:34:34.730 --> 00:34:36.630
Affleck writing Good Will Hunting.
阿弗莱克创作《心灵捕手》的故事。

789
00:34:37.170 --> 00:34:45.030
And Mindy played Ben Affleck and Brenda, who's in Booze Cruise, played Matt Damon.
敏迪演本·阿弗莱克，而出演《酒醉游轮》的布伦达演马特·达蒙。

790
00:34:45.230 --> 00:34:46.830
And it was a hilarious play.
那是一部非常搞笑的剧。

791
00:34:46.990 --> 00:34:47.930
You went and saw it?
你去看过吗？

792
00:34:47.990 --> 00:34:48.670
Yes, I went and saw it.
是的，我去看过。

793
00:34:48.670 --> 00:34:50.170
By accident or on purpose?
是偶然还是特意去的？

794
00:34:50.170 --> 00:34:57.170
No, I was actually, I was a guest of my wife, Suzanne Daniels, who was a network executive,
不，其实我是作为我妻子苏珊·丹尼尔斯的客人去的，她当时是电视台高管，

795
00:34:57.170 --> 00:34:58.810
possibly at the WB at that time.
可能当时是在WB电视台工作。

796
00:34:58.810 --> 00:35:00.330
I'm not exactly sure where she was working.
我不确定她当时具体在哪里工作。

797
00:35:00.550 --> 00:35:04.890
And she went to see it to do talent scouting.
她是去那里进行人才发掘的。

798
00:35:05.290 --> 00:35:07.910
And I thought it was super funny.
我觉得那部剧超级好笑。

799
00:35:08.410 --> 00:35:09.630
And it was great.
非常棒。

800
00:35:09.830 --> 00:35:17.290
And then by coincidence, Mindy's spec script came in like the next day for me to read for
然后巧合的是，第二天敏迪的样片剧本就送到我手里让我阅读了。

801
00:35:17.290 --> 00:35:18.210
staffing for writers.
编剧人员配置。

802
00:35:18.210 --> 00:35:20.030
So I was like, hey, wait, that's the one I just saw.
所以我当时就想，嘿，等等，那不是我刚看到的那个吗。

803
00:35:21.110 --> 00:35:21.470
Amazing.
太棒了。

804
00:35:21.710 --> 00:35:21.910
Yeah.
是啊。

805
00:35:22.490 --> 00:35:22.850
Amazing.
太棒了。

806
00:35:23.010 --> 00:35:23.290
Terrific.
好极了。

807
00:35:23.730 --> 00:35:24.050
Wow.
哇。

808
00:35:24.050 --> 00:35:25.210
I would have loved to seen that.
我真希望能看到那个。

809
00:35:25.410 --> 00:35:29.050
So now we have Brenda, and she's like the corporate person.
现在我们有了布伦达，她就像是公司派来的人。

810
00:35:29.250 --> 00:35:31.390
You guys, I just have to point out something about Brenda.
伙计们，我必须指出关于布伦达的一点。

811
00:35:31.650 --> 00:35:35.590
I know we're not on the boat yet, but Brenda drinks the whole boat ride.
我知道我们还没上船，但布伦达在整个乘船过程中都在喝酒。

812
00:35:36.670 --> 00:35:38.530
She's there to check in on Michael.
她是来查看迈克尔的情况的。

813
00:35:38.770 --> 00:35:40.110
She has a beer in her hand.
她手里一直拿着啤酒。

814
00:35:40.250 --> 00:35:40.670
You look.
你们看。

815
00:35:40.750 --> 00:35:42.230
Look at her scenes on the boat.
看看她在船上的那些镜头。

816
00:35:42.410 --> 00:35:44.010
She has a beer the whole time.
她全程都拿着啤酒。

817
00:35:44.150 --> 00:35:44.910
She's at the bar.
她一直在吧台那儿。

818
00:35:45.090 --> 00:35:47.270
I mean, he only sees her when she's at the bar, pretty much.
我是说，他基本上只有在吧台看到她。

819
00:35:47.330 --> 00:35:47.830
Pretty much.
差不多吧。

820
00:35:47.830 --> 00:35:51.230
Or she walks up with a beer to check in on him.
或者她拿着啤酒走过来查看他的情况。

821
00:35:51.630 --> 00:35:55.050
Wait, before we get out of the conference room scene, Phyllis broke so hard.
等等，在离开会议室场景之前，菲利斯笑场得太厉害了。

822
00:35:55.210 --> 00:35:56.130
Do you remember this?
你还记得吗？

823
00:35:56.710 --> 00:35:57.370
Oh, yes.
哦，记得。

824
00:35:57.370 --> 00:35:58.130
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

825
00:35:58.250 --> 00:35:58.410
Yes.
记得。

826
00:35:58.410 --> 00:36:03.330
So Michael has said that the sales team could be, it's like the furnace of the ship.
迈克尔说销售团队就像是船上的锅炉。

827
00:36:03.490 --> 00:36:03.730
Yes.
没错。

828
00:36:04.050 --> 00:36:06.130
Because it keeps things moving along.
因为他们让事情得以推进。

829
00:36:06.210 --> 00:36:06.430
Yes.
没错。

830
00:36:06.630 --> 00:36:10.330
And he compares them to the people from Titanic.
他还把他们比作《泰坦尼克号》里的人。

831
00:36:10.670 --> 00:36:11.010
Right.
对。

832
00:36:11.310 --> 00:36:11.630
Titanic.
《泰坦尼克号》。

833
00:36:11.990 --> 00:36:16.390
And at five minutes, 20 seconds, Phyllis has to put her head down because she starts laughing
在5分20秒的时候，菲利斯不得不低下头，因为她开始笑了。

834
00:36:16.390 --> 00:36:19.610
because she says, she asked what the furnace does.
因为她说，她问锅炉是干什么用的。

835
00:36:19.610 --> 00:36:24.050
And then at five minutes, 50 seconds, she says, everyone in the engine room drowned.
然后在5分50秒的时候，她说，机舱里的所有人都淹死了。

836
00:36:24.590 --> 00:36:25.210
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

837
00:36:25.210 --> 00:36:25.490
Yes.
记得。

838
00:36:25.490 --> 00:36:27.510
She could not get out the word drown.
她就是说不出“淹死”这个词。

839
00:36:27.810 --> 00:36:28.630
Like, she couldn't.
就是说不出来。

840
00:36:28.710 --> 00:36:29.990
She just broke every time.
她每次都笑场。

841
00:36:29.990 --> 00:36:32.570
And you can see her, like, starting to break.
你可以看到她开始憋不住笑。

842
00:36:32.570 --> 00:36:35.010
That made me break on the day.
那天我也被她逗笑了。

843
00:36:35.190 --> 00:36:35.950
Yes, me too.
是啊，我也是。

844
00:36:36.490 --> 00:36:39.890
When Phyllis so sadly realized that everyone in the engine room drowned.
当菲利斯悲伤地意识到机舱里的所有人都淹死的时候。

845
00:36:40.270 --> 00:36:41.730
She's like, but Michael, everyone drowned.
她说，可是迈克尔，所有人都淹死了。

846
00:36:42.150 --> 00:36:46.290
Well, now let's, we have to have the moment everyone gets on the boat.
好了，现在我们得聊聊大家上船的那一刻了。

847
00:36:46.430 --> 00:36:47.850
We've left the conference room.
我们已经离开会议室了。

848
00:36:47.990 --> 00:36:48.290
Yes.
是的。

849
00:36:48.430 --> 00:36:49.450
We're jumping around a little.
我们跳跃得有点多。

850
00:36:49.910 --> 00:36:54.730
At six minutes, 20 seconds, Michael says that Pam is Mary Ann.
在6分20秒的时候，迈克尔说帕姆是玛丽·安。

851
00:36:55.270 --> 00:36:57.310
Katie and Jim are the professor and Ginger.
凯蒂和吉姆分别是教授和金格。

852
00:36:57.910 --> 00:36:59.030
Angela's Mrs. Howell.
安吉拉是豪威尔夫人。

853
00:36:59.550 --> 00:37:00.390
Kelly's the native.
凯莉是土著人。

854
00:37:00.950 --> 00:37:02.770
Stanley is one of the globetrotters.
斯坦利是环球旅行者之一。

855
00:37:02.990 --> 00:37:03.850
Michael is a skipper.
迈克尔是船长。

856
00:37:03.990 --> 00:37:04.930
And Dwight is Gilligan.
而德怀特是吉利根。

857
00:37:05.130 --> 00:37:09.370
And this begins the war between Captain Jack and Captain Michael.
于是杰克船长和迈克尔船长之间的战争开始了。

858
00:37:09.710 --> 00:37:10.150
Yes.
是的。

859
00:37:10.250 --> 00:37:15.430
I love that Michael has worn his captain hat to the booze cruise.
我喜欢迈克尔戴着他的船长帽来参加游船派对。

860
00:37:15.870 --> 00:37:18.450
He has it on in the booze cruise and he still has it on.
他在游船派对上戴着它，现在还戴着。

861
00:37:18.590 --> 00:37:20.870
And now they're having their little power struggle.
现在他们正在进行小小的权力斗争。

862
00:37:21.130 --> 00:37:23.890
Who is going to be the boss of this trip?
谁才是这次旅行的老大？

863
00:37:24.610 --> 00:37:26.810
Captain Jack is clearly going to win.
杰克船长显然会赢。

864
00:37:26.810 --> 00:37:30.410
And I mean, I feel like his boundary is very strong from the beginning.
我的意思是，我觉得他从一开始就划定了非常明确的界限。

865
00:37:30.590 --> 00:37:31.110
Very strong.
非常明确。

866
00:37:31.270 --> 00:37:31.970
And I want you to know-
我想让你知道——

867
00:37:31.970 --> 00:37:34.030
We should say, Captain Jack played by Rob Riggle.
我们应该提一下，杰克船长由罗伯·里格尔饰演。

868
00:37:34.170 --> 00:37:34.450
Yes.
是的。

869
00:37:34.710 --> 00:37:35.410
Who was a Marine.
他曾是一名海军陆战队员。

870
00:37:35.610 --> 00:37:35.850
Yes.
是的。

871
00:37:35.850 --> 00:37:36.410
Who was a Marine.
他曾是一名海军陆战队员。

872
00:37:36.510 --> 00:37:36.770
Yes.
是的。

873
00:37:36.950 --> 00:37:37.070
Yes.
是的。

874
00:37:37.070 --> 00:37:41.670
So there's a lot of authenticity to Captain Jack's military bearing there.
所以杰克船长的军人风范非常有真实感。

875
00:37:41.670 --> 00:37:42.830
How did you find Rob?
你是怎么找到罗伯的？

876
00:37:43.490 --> 00:37:45.310
Well, I mean, you know Rob, right?
嗯，我的意思是，你认识罗伯，对吧？

877
00:37:45.390 --> 00:37:46.030
I know Rob.
我认识罗伯。

878
00:37:46.170 --> 00:37:48.490
We talked a little bit about it in one of our Fast Facts.
我们在其中一个“快速事实”里简单聊过这个。

879
00:37:48.630 --> 00:37:51.150
But Rob wanted me to give you a message.
但罗伯让我给你带个话。

880
00:37:51.270 --> 00:37:51.470
Yeah.
嗯。

881
00:37:51.510 --> 00:37:52.390
Because I talked to him yesterday.
因为我昨天和他聊过。

882
00:37:52.650 --> 00:37:54.470
And he said, thank you so much.
他说，非常感谢你。

883
00:37:54.910 --> 00:37:57.650
Also, he's sorry that he couldn't say Lake Wallenpaw back.
另外，他很抱歉当时没能接上“沃伦帕克湖”这个梗。

884
00:37:59.690 --> 00:38:02.430
Rob was, you know, in the Alison Jones orbit.
罗伯当时在艾莉森·琼斯的圈子里。

885
00:38:02.630 --> 00:38:03.010
Yeah.
是的。

886
00:38:03.070 --> 00:38:05.710
So, and we certainly knew about him.
所以，我们当然知道他。

887
00:38:06.510 --> 00:38:10.250
And I don't know whether he came in for one of the other parts.
我不确定他是否来试镜过其他角色。

888
00:38:10.390 --> 00:38:12.150
Like, he might have come in for Dwight or something.
比如，他可能来试镜过德怀特之类的角色。

889
00:38:12.290 --> 00:38:13.330
I'm not 100% sure.
我不敢百分之百确定。

890
00:38:13.610 --> 00:38:14.570
Did that happen sometimes?
这种情况时有发生吗？

891
00:38:14.610 --> 00:38:18.790
People who had come in for main cast members, you would ping them for a future episode?
对于那些来试镜主要角色的演员，你们会把他们留作未来剧集的候选人吗？

892
00:38:19.030 --> 00:38:19.290
Sure.
当然。

893
00:38:19.290 --> 00:38:19.730
Yeah.
是的。

894
00:38:19.990 --> 00:38:26.150
I mean, I think Alison released some of the audition tapes as part of a DVD extra.
我的意思是，我觉得艾莉森把一些试镜录像作为DVD花絮发布了。

895
00:38:26.470 --> 00:38:28.630
But there were a lot of cool people that came in.
当时有很多很棒的人来试镜。

896
00:38:28.690 --> 00:38:31.170
It would have been very interesting to see Seth Rogen as Dwight, for instance.
比如，如果能看到塞斯·罗根演德怀特，那会非常有趣。

897
00:38:31.550 --> 00:38:32.250
Yes, definitely.
是的，绝对。

898
00:38:32.930 --> 00:38:34.470
Or Kristen Wiig as Pam.
或者克里斯汀·韦格演帕姆。

899
00:38:34.550 --> 00:38:34.730
Yeah.
是的。

900
00:38:34.810 --> 00:38:36.150
I think she came in to read Pam.
我想她是来试读帕姆这个角色的。

901
00:38:36.410 --> 00:38:36.570
Yeah.
是啊。

902
00:38:36.630 --> 00:38:39.590
I think she's in my, on my, on my, Alison Jones.
我想她是在我的，在我的，在我的，艾莉森·琼斯那儿。

903
00:38:39.650 --> 00:38:40.050
And Catherine Hahn.
还有凯瑟琳·哈恩。

904
00:38:40.250 --> 00:38:40.430
Yeah.
是啊。

905
00:38:40.890 --> 00:38:42.990
Alison Jones gave me my sign-in sheet day.
艾莉森·琼斯给了我当天的签到表。

906
00:38:43.230 --> 00:38:45.870
And Catherine Hahn is on it.
凯瑟琳·哈恩也在上面。

907
00:38:46.050 --> 00:38:47.370
And Bob Odenkirk is on it.
鲍勃·奥登科克也在上面。

908
00:38:47.430 --> 00:38:47.570
Yeah.
是啊。

909
00:38:47.570 --> 00:38:50.310
Well, Bob was really the number two.
嗯，鲍勃确实是第二人选。

910
00:38:50.410 --> 00:38:52.770
If we didn't have Steve, it would have been Bob.
如果我们没有史蒂夫，那就会是鲍勃了。

911
00:38:52.850 --> 00:38:53.630
He did a great job.
他表现得非常出色。

912
00:38:53.770 --> 00:38:56.750
And then in season nine, we brought him back as the sort of echo.
然后在第九季，我们让他回来扮演了一个类似回声的角色。

913
00:38:56.950 --> 00:38:58.810
He was so fantastic, too.
他也表现得太棒了。

914
00:38:58.990 --> 00:38:59.130
Yeah.
是啊。

915
00:38:59.990 --> 00:39:00.670
He's great.
他很棒。

916
00:39:00.870 --> 00:39:03.690
So I have a lot of fan questions about the boat.
所以我有很多粉丝关于那艘船的问题。

917
00:39:03.890 --> 00:39:04.150
Sure.
当然。

918
00:39:04.330 --> 00:39:04.570
Okay.
好的。

919
00:39:04.950 --> 00:39:10.250
So since we're getting on the boat, Casey Wright asked, was the boat really moving?
既然我们要聊到船，凯西·赖特问，那艘船是真的在动吗？

920
00:39:10.310 --> 00:39:13.170
And Sam Pellett asked how cold it was.
山姆·佩莱特问当时有多冷。

921
00:39:13.310 --> 00:39:16.590
The boat was really moving through the water for one of the days of shooting.
拍摄的那几天里，有一天船确实是在水面上航行的。

922
00:39:16.590 --> 00:39:18.590
The other two days, I believe it was docked.
另外两天，我想它是停靠在岸边的。

923
00:39:18.810 --> 00:39:20.070
And it was cold.
而且确实很冷。

924
00:39:20.070 --> 00:39:25.150
It was December 2005, which was chilly, especially at night out on the water.
那是2005年12月，天气很冷，尤其是在水面上过夜的时候。

925
00:39:25.350 --> 00:39:28.930
A lot of people wondered, were you pretending to be that cold?
很多人好奇，你们当时是在假装那么冷吗？

926
00:39:29.330 --> 00:39:31.010
I remember being cold.
我记得当时真的很冷。

927
00:39:31.170 --> 00:39:31.370
Yes.
是的。

928
00:39:31.730 --> 00:39:33.230
I don't think there was a lot of pretending.
我觉得没怎么假装。

929
00:39:33.230 --> 00:39:35.890
Your cheeks are like bright pink in that scene.
那一幕里你的脸颊红得像苹果一样。

930
00:39:36.070 --> 00:39:36.430
Yes.
是的。

931
00:39:36.750 --> 00:39:45.190
So Lorne Michaels has a thing that he says sometimes where he will get in-character underwear for the actors.
洛恩·迈克尔斯有时会有一个习惯，他会为演员准备符合角色设定的内衣。

932
00:39:45.710 --> 00:39:45.990
Oh.
哦。

933
00:39:47.030 --> 00:39:47.470
Yeah.
是啊。

934
00:39:47.470 --> 00:39:48.470
I think this is it.
我想就是这个。

935
00:39:49.170 --> 00:39:50.570
And people will say, well, why?
人们会问，嗯，为什么？

936
00:39:50.670 --> 00:39:51.110
Who cares?
谁会在意呢？

937
00:39:51.250 --> 00:39:52.330
It's not going to be on camera.
反正镜头又拍不到。

938
00:39:52.390 --> 00:39:53.610
And he goes, yes, but the actors know.
他会说，是的，但演员们自己知道。

939
00:39:54.610 --> 00:39:55.850
I kind of get that.
我有点理解这一点。

940
00:39:55.910 --> 00:39:56.070
Yeah.
是啊。

941
00:39:56.070 --> 00:39:57.470
I kind of get that.
我有点理解这一点。

942
00:39:57.570 --> 00:40:03.470
And so we certainly believed in that and went out on this real boat in Long Beach Harbor and it was this huge thing.
所以我们当然相信这一点，并去了长滩港那艘真正的船上拍摄，那是一件大事。

943
00:40:03.730 --> 00:40:13.390
And to me, the key of it was that romantic scene on the top deck between Pam and Jim.
对我来说，关键在于帕姆和吉姆在顶层甲板上的那场浪漫戏。

944
00:40:15.510 --> 00:40:20.990
And I just thought it'd be so pretty up there with the twinkling lights of the harbor in the background and everything.
我当时觉得，在那儿拍摄，背景是港口闪烁的灯光，一切都会非常美。

945
00:40:20.990 --> 00:40:28.750
So we do that scene and later in the editing room, somebody was like, what'd you do?
所以我们拍了那场戏，后来在剪辑室里，有人问，你们做了什么？

946
00:40:28.870 --> 00:40:34.870
Did you just put a row of Christmas lights against a black piece of duvetyne there and do it in a studio?
你们是不是只是在摄影棚里，在黑色的遮光布前挂了一串圣诞灯拍的？

947
00:40:34.970 --> 00:40:35.530
And we're like, no.
我们说，没有。

948
00:40:36.810 --> 00:40:38.150
We're on a boat.
我们在船上。

949
00:40:38.310 --> 00:40:39.350
We're on an actual boat.
我们在真正的船上。

950
00:40:39.430 --> 00:40:42.450
But it didn't really look that impressive when it came down.
但拍出来之后，看起来确实没那么震撼。

951
00:40:42.570 --> 00:40:46.590
It was just this one little twinkle thing of lights on the horizon.
地平线上只有那一点点微弱的灯光。

952
00:40:46.870 --> 00:40:47.910
Like we could have been on a soundstage.
感觉就像我们身处摄影棚一样。

953
00:40:47.910 --> 00:40:48.090
Yeah.
是啊。

954
00:40:48.090 --> 00:40:49.950
We could have been nice and toasty and comfortable.
我们本可以舒舒服服、暖暖和和的。

955
00:40:49.950 --> 00:40:52.410
But the wind was blowing and I don't know.
但风一直在吹，我也不知道怎么说。

956
00:40:52.490 --> 00:40:53.510
I could tell you're on a boat.
我看得出你们在船上。

957
00:40:53.650 --> 00:40:54.390
I think so.
我想也是。

958
00:40:54.790 --> 00:40:57.730
Well, one of the challenges of being on the boat was how sick everyone got.
嗯，在船上的一大挑战就是大家都晕船晕得厉害。

959
00:40:57.870 --> 00:40:58.850
Greg, do you remember that?
格雷格，你还记得吗？

960
00:40:59.290 --> 00:40:59.870
We were all really sick.
我们当时都病得很重。

961
00:40:59.870 --> 00:41:01.070
Yeah, there was a lot of seasickness.
没错，晕船的人特别多。

962
00:41:01.390 --> 00:41:02.990
Rain peaked a lot.
雷恩吐得最厉害。

963
00:41:03.310 --> 00:41:03.490
Yeah.
是啊。

964
00:41:04.730 --> 00:41:14.410
I did not get seasick, but do you remember coming up to Kate Flannery and I and saying, hey, you guys, I want to get some B-roll of people vomiting off the side of the boat?
我没晕船，但你还记得你走过来对我和凯特·弗兰纳里说，嘿，你们几个，我想拍些大家在船边呕吐的空镜素材吗？

965
00:41:14.590 --> 00:41:15.210
Greg, do you remember?
格雷格，你记得吗？

966
00:41:15.210 --> 00:41:16.850
I don't, but that would be something I would have done.
我不记得了，但这确实是我会干出来的事。

967
00:41:16.850 --> 00:41:25.530
It was like three in the morning and you said, so you had Matt Stone grab as many people as he could and we had the choice of cream of mushroom or minestrone.
当时大概是凌晨三点，你说要马特·斯通尽可能多找些人，我们当时有奶油蘑菇汤和蔬菜汤可选。

968
00:41:25.950 --> 00:41:26.930
Oh, right, right, right.
哦，对对对。

969
00:41:27.110 --> 00:41:27.830
The fake vomiting.
假装呕吐。

970
00:41:28.090 --> 00:41:28.610
The fake vomiting.
假装呕吐。

971
00:41:28.750 --> 00:41:29.410
The fake vomiting.
假装呕吐。

972
00:41:29.670 --> 00:41:32.130
And I did minestrone.
我选了蔬菜汤。

973
00:41:32.330 --> 00:41:33.090
Yeah, good choice.
嗯，选得好。

974
00:41:33.090 --> 00:41:38.910
You had to take a swig of it and hold it in your mouth until action and then puke it.
你得喝上一大口，含在嘴里，直到导演喊开始，然后把它吐出来。

975
00:41:39.270 --> 00:41:48.630
And the, I don't know, five to ten seconds you held it in your mouth was the most horrible thing because you were just like, like trying not to gag.
那含在嘴里的五到十秒简直太痛苦了，因为你得拼命忍住不反胃。

976
00:41:49.030 --> 00:41:52.910
So I didn't puke for real, but I did fake puke.
所以我没真吐，但我确实假吐了。

977
00:41:53.030 --> 00:41:54.510
Well, I got really sick.
我当时真的病得很重。

978
00:41:54.650 --> 00:41:55.510
So did David Denman.
大卫·丹曼也是。

979
00:41:56.730 --> 00:41:58.770
And I was wearing those wristbands.
我当时还戴着那种防晕船手环。

980
00:41:59.090 --> 00:41:59.370
Yes.
没错。

981
00:41:59.590 --> 00:42:01.730
We were trying to pass out boning too or stuff.
我们当时还试着分发晕船药之类的东西。

982
00:42:01.970 --> 00:42:05.030
Yeah, there was all, there were all these remedies, but nothing really worked.
是啊，当时各种偏方都有，但都没什么用。

983
00:42:05.290 --> 00:42:05.890
Seasickness, gum.
晕船口香糖。

984
00:42:05.890 --> 00:42:07.350
Someone gave me something to chew on.
有人给了我一些嚼的东西。

985
00:42:07.830 --> 00:42:08.750
Maybe the gum.
可能就是那种口香糖。

986
00:42:08.990 --> 00:42:09.110
Yeah.
是啊。

987
00:42:09.230 --> 00:42:10.430
There's like a ginger gum.
有一种姜味口香糖。

988
00:42:10.610 --> 00:42:10.870
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

989
00:42:11.050 --> 00:42:16.890
So at one point, the real captain of the boat heard that I was struggling.
有一次，真正的船长听说我很难受。

990
00:42:17.250 --> 00:42:17.410
So there were three captains.
当时有三位船长。

991
00:42:17.470 --> 00:42:18.190
There were three captains.
确实有三位船长。

992
00:42:19.110 --> 00:42:25.270
And then there was also, there was Dwight steering the ship and a guy and then a real guy.
还有德怀特在掌舵，旁边有个伙计，还有一个真正的船员。

993
00:42:25.690 --> 00:42:34.230
At one point, the real captain of the ship heard I was struggling and he got out this oil that he rubbed behind my ears.
有一次，真正的船长听说我很难受，他拿出一瓶精油，抹在我耳朵后面。

994
00:42:35.070 --> 00:42:37.870
And about ten minutes later, I was totally fine.
大约十分钟后，我就完全没事了。

995
00:42:38.210 --> 00:42:38.590
Wow.
哇。

996
00:42:38.730 --> 00:42:40.350
So I had written about this in my diary.
我当时还在日记里写过这件事。

997
00:42:40.350 --> 00:42:42.530
I looked it up and I found some on Amazon.
我查了一下，在亚马逊上找到了同款。

998
00:42:42.810 --> 00:42:43.870
Here's what's in it.
这就是它的成分。

999
00:42:44.210 --> 00:42:47.430
Here's where we turn this whole thing into an essential oils pitch.
现在我们要把这整件事变成一场精油推销了。

1000
00:42:47.430 --> 00:42:47.870
Yes.
没错。

1001
00:42:48.190 --> 00:42:48.770
That's right.
没错。

1002
00:42:48.790 --> 00:42:49.230
Pitch podcaSt.
推销播客。

1003
00:42:49.490 --> 00:42:50.130
By the way.
顺便说一下。

1004
00:42:50.290 --> 00:42:51.650
We're sponsored by.
我们由……赞助。

1005
00:42:51.810 --> 00:42:51.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1006
00:42:52.390 --> 00:42:53.410
Sold by Jan.
简（Jan）卖的。

1007
00:42:53.830 --> 00:42:55.430
Jan's essential oils and candles.
简的精油和蜡烛。

1008
00:42:55.730 --> 00:42:56.730
So here's what it has in it.
所以这里面有这些东西。

1009
00:42:57.110 --> 00:43:07.490
Lavender, peppermint, chamomile, something called ylang-ylang, birch, and then it has frankincense and myrrh.
薰衣草、薄荷、洋甘菊、一种叫依兰的东西、桦木，还有乳香和没药。

1010
00:43:07.750 --> 00:43:10.210
That's the stuff that the wise men gave to Jesus.
那是智者送给耶稣的东西。

1011
00:43:10.530 --> 00:43:10.970
Yeah, I know.
是啊，我知道。

1012
00:43:11.070 --> 00:43:11.830
Two of the things.
其中两样。

1013
00:43:12.170 --> 00:43:13.030
Very expensive stuff.
非常昂贵的东西。

1014
00:43:13.150 --> 00:43:13.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1015
00:43:13.670 --> 00:43:13.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1016
00:43:14.290 --> 00:43:14.810
Fancy.
真高级。

1017
00:43:15.070 --> 00:43:15.550
Who knew?
谁知道呢？

1018
00:43:18.190 --> 00:43:20.310
Circumstance and myrrh are real, but.
乳香和没药是真实存在的，但是。

1019
00:43:20.430 --> 00:43:21.470
I didn't know they were real.
我以前不知道它们是真实存在的。

1020
00:43:21.770 --> 00:43:22.150
I mean.
我是说。

1021
00:43:22.570 --> 00:43:24.510
I thought they were part of a Christmas song.
我以为它们只是圣诞歌曲里的一部分。

1022
00:43:24.970 --> 00:43:25.950
That's not real.
那不是真的。

1023
00:43:26.190 --> 00:43:28.290
But like, what are they?
但它们到底是什么呢？

1024
00:43:28.470 --> 00:43:30.950
I guess they are what you rub behind your ears when you're seasick.
我猜它们是你晕船时涂在耳后用的东西。

1025
00:43:30.950 --> 00:43:34.350
It sounds like they just threw everything in the kitchen sink into this.
听起来他们就像把厨房水槽里的所有东西都扔进去了。

1026
00:43:34.450 --> 00:43:34.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1027
00:43:34.950 --> 00:43:35.000
They did.
他们确实这么做了。

1028
00:43:35.410 --> 00:43:36.610
The ylang-ylang?
依兰？

1029
00:43:36.770 --> 00:43:37.430
I don't know.
我不知道。

1030
00:43:37.650 --> 00:43:37.910
Ylang-ylang.
依兰。

1031
00:43:37.970 --> 00:43:38.830
Ylang-ylang.
依兰。

1032
00:43:39.110 --> 00:43:39.530
All right.
好吧。

1033
00:43:39.630 --> 00:43:47.450
So in the script, there was a scene, Greg, that as the boat is pulling away, Toby's car suddenly drives up.
在剧本里，格雷格，有一场戏是当船开走时，托比的车突然开了过来。

1034
00:43:48.310 --> 00:43:54.530
And he, and Michael yells at him from the ship, oh, come on, what's up?
然后他，迈克尔在船上对他大喊，噢，得了吧，怎么了？

1035
00:43:54.590 --> 00:43:58.070
And he's like, I'm sorry, there was an accident or there was traffic.
他说，抱歉，出了点事故或者堵车了。

1036
00:43:58.390 --> 00:44:00.490
And then Michael says, we're not going back.
然后迈克尔说，我们不会回去的。

1037
00:44:00.610 --> 00:44:01.410
We're not going back for him.
我们不会为了他回去的。

1038
00:44:01.450 --> 00:44:02.090
Just leave him.
就把他留在那儿。

1039
00:44:02.330 --> 00:44:06.730
And then Paul turns to camera as Toby and he kind of gives a little wink.
然后保罗作为托比转向镜头，他给了个小暗示。

1040
00:44:06.770 --> 00:44:07.410
Yeah, it's a big smile.
是啊，是一个大大的微笑。

1041
00:44:07.430 --> 00:44:08.250
Yeah, like he did it on purpose.
是啊，就像他是故意的一样。

1042
00:44:08.430 --> 00:44:10.070
But you can find that in the deleted scenes.
但你可以在删减片段里找到那一幕。

1043
00:44:10.110 --> 00:44:10.710
We shot it.
我们拍了。

1044
00:44:10.790 --> 00:44:11.030
Yes.
是的。

1045
00:44:11.150 --> 00:44:11.710
We shot it.
我们拍了。

1046
00:44:11.730 --> 00:44:12.310
And it was very nice.
而且拍得很好。

1047
00:44:12.310 --> 00:44:15.450
And that is why Toby is not on the boat for anyone who was wondering.
这就是为什么托比不在船上的原因，如果有谁好奇的话。

1048
00:44:15.950 --> 00:44:16.570
Maybe we should take a boat.
也许我们应该坐船。

1049
00:44:16.570 --> 00:44:23.230
There's a lot of excuses for why Toby wouldn't be on things so that he could help out as a writer and producer.
托比之所以不在场，有很多借口，这样他就能以编剧和制片人的身份帮忙了。

1050
00:44:23.790 --> 00:44:25.670
Toby and BJ and Mindy.
托比、BJ和敏迪。

1051
00:44:25.870 --> 00:44:25.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1052
00:44:25.990 --> 00:44:28.410
Like they sat in the, you know, Mindy was in the annex.
就像他们坐在，你知道的，明迪当时在侧厅。

1053
00:44:28.730 --> 00:44:28.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1054
00:44:28.850 --> 00:44:29.170
Things like that.
诸如此类的事情。

1055
00:44:29.170 --> 00:44:35.410
I thought I was so clever in season one making them actors so that they would have this experience of being actors.
我在第一季时自作聪明，把他们设定成演员，这样他们就能有当演员的体验。

1056
00:44:35.430 --> 00:44:41.530
And then at some point in season two, I'm looking around and 50% of the writers are gone because they're on set.
结果到了第二季某个时候，我环顾四周，发现50%的编剧都不见了，因为他们都在片场。

1057
00:44:41.530 --> 00:44:42.690
And I'm like, oh, what have I done?
当时我就想，噢，我到底干了什么？

1058
00:44:45.230 --> 00:44:45.670
Okay.
好的。

1059
00:44:45.810 --> 00:44:49.190
At seven minutes, 55 seconds, Rob Riggle breaks.
在7分55秒的时候，罗伯·里格尔笑场了。

1060
00:44:49.390 --> 00:44:50.490
He totally breaks.
他彻底笑场了。

1061
00:44:50.710 --> 00:44:50.870
What?
什么？

1062
00:44:51.010 --> 00:44:51.750
We talked about it.
我们讨论过这个。

1063
00:44:51.810 --> 00:44:53.530
It just, it stayed in the shot.
它就那样，留在了镜头里。

1064
00:44:53.770 --> 00:44:58.150
So Rob as Captain Jack is going over the safety features of the boat.
当时罗伯饰演的杰克船长正在讲解船上的安全设施。

1065
00:44:58.730 --> 00:45:02.170
And Michael really wants to hijack this speech and give it.
迈克尔非常想抢过这段演讲自己来说。

1066
00:45:02.310 --> 00:45:03.670
And he can't.
但他做不到。

1067
00:45:03.770 --> 00:45:07.210
So he just starts doing like the flight attendant, like pointing to the exits.
所以他开始像空乘人员那样，指着出口方向。

1068
00:45:07.430 --> 00:45:07.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1069
00:45:07.770 --> 00:45:08.830
And Rob just breaks.
然后罗伯就笑场了。

1070
00:45:09.090 --> 00:45:10.990
He just starts laughing, but he just keeps going.
他开始大笑，但他还是坚持演了下去。

1071
00:45:11.530 --> 00:45:13.130
And then Rain is Dwight laughs.
接着雷恩饰演的德怀特也笑了。

1072
00:45:13.330 --> 00:45:15.390
And so it just sort of like, but it stays in.
所以就变成了那样，但镜头还是保留了下来。

1073
00:45:15.550 --> 00:45:16.490
Oh, that's amazing.
噢，那太棒了。

1074
00:45:16.790 --> 00:45:18.870
But Rob was like, yeah, I just laughed.
罗伯当时说，是啊，我就是笑了。

1075
00:45:18.890 --> 00:45:21.090
And I, but I just kept talking through my laugh.
但我还是边笑边把台词说完了。

1076
00:45:21.370 --> 00:45:23.450
When Steve is doing his dancing.
当史蒂夫在跳舞的时候。

1077
00:45:23.730 --> 00:45:24.130
Yes.
没错。

1078
00:45:24.330 --> 00:45:32.990
That I remember like trying to build the reactions because everybody's supposed to be like unimpressed and just, you know, straight faced.
我记得当时在努力铺垫大家的反应，因为每个人都应该表现得不为所动，你知道的，面无表情。

1079
00:45:32.990 --> 00:45:39.590
And, uh, it was almost impossible because everybody was breaking and made him do that over and over and over again.
呃，这几乎是不可能的，因为每个人都在笑场，让他一遍又一遍地重复那个动作。

1080
00:45:39.750 --> 00:45:41.030
For so long.
持续了很久。

1081
00:45:41.110 --> 00:45:41.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1082
00:45:41.230 --> 00:45:47.610
That's, I remember, I was, I remember when we rewatched it, I just wrote, oh my gosh, Michael's dance because he danced for so long.
我记得，我记得当我们重温这一集时，我写道，天哪，迈克尔的舞，因为他跳了太久了。

1083
00:45:47.610 --> 00:45:51.350
In my journal, I said that we started taping that around 2 a.m.
在我的日记里，我说过我们大约凌晨两点开始录制那段戏。

1084
00:45:51.470 --> 00:45:53.070
Like it was really late.
真的很晚了。

1085
00:45:53.510 --> 00:45:53.810
Yeah.
是啊。

1086
00:45:54.070 --> 00:45:56.970
A fan question from Tara Leitchkey.
来自塔拉·莱奇基的粉丝提问。

1087
00:45:57.730 --> 00:46:00.350
Was Steve's dance choreographed?
史蒂夫的舞蹈是编排好的吗？

1088
00:46:01.110 --> 00:46:02.270
I don't think so.
我觉得不是。

1089
00:46:02.490 --> 00:46:04.190
I really think he improvised that.
我真的觉得他是即兴发挥的。

1090
00:46:04.210 --> 00:46:06.190
I don't remember it being in the script.
我不记得剧本里有写。

1091
00:46:06.410 --> 00:46:08.970
I think he just kind of went for it.
我觉得他就是随性发挥的。

1092
00:46:09.150 --> 00:46:15.210
I have the script at home for this episode and I read it and there is no direction for Michael's dance in the script.
我家里有这一集的剧本，我读过，剧本里对迈克尔的舞蹈没有任何指导说明。

1093
00:46:15.430 --> 00:46:18.790
It just says, pan over to see Michael doing a weird dance.
上面只写了，镜头摇过去，看到迈克尔在跳一段奇怪的舞。

1094
00:46:18.950 --> 00:46:19.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1095
00:46:19.410 --> 00:46:19.790
That's it.
就这些。

1096
00:46:19.930 --> 00:46:22.410
That's as much as there was.
剧本里就只有这么多。

1097
00:46:22.910 --> 00:46:24.670
Another fan question about the dance.
另一个关于舞蹈的粉丝提问。

1098
00:46:24.670 --> 00:46:32.270
Steve Dresser says, how many takes of that superb dance did it take to get Steve's full moves?
史蒂夫·德雷瑟问，那段精彩的舞蹈拍了多少条才捕捉到史蒂夫的全套动作？

1099
00:46:32.530 --> 00:46:34.370
I'm going to say about six, I think.
我想大概拍了六条吧。

1100
00:46:34.510 --> 00:46:34.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1101
00:46:34.850 --> 00:46:35.470
What do you think?
你觉得怎么样？

1102
00:46:35.590 --> 00:46:36.170
What do you remember?
你还记得什么？

1103
00:46:36.470 --> 00:46:37.590
That seems about right.
那看起来差不多。

1104
00:46:37.830 --> 00:46:40.950
I can't remember when he started slapping his legs.
我不记得他是什么时候开始拍大腿的了。

1105
00:46:40.950 --> 00:46:41.950
Yeah, that was amazing.
是啊，那太棒了。

1106
00:46:42.070 --> 00:46:43.830
If that was early on or later.
不知道那是早期还是后期。

1107
00:46:44.110 --> 00:46:44.890
And the worm.
还有那个蠕虫舞。

1108
00:46:45.050 --> 00:46:45.890
I mean, they were different.
我是说，它们是不一样的。

1109
00:46:45.890 --> 00:46:50.510
I feel like there were different versions of the dance and then we kind of made the highlight reel.
我觉得舞蹈有不同的版本，然后我们整理出了精华片段。

1110
00:46:50.770 --> 00:46:50.950
Yes.
是的。

1111
00:46:54.810 --> 00:46:56.790
Of the dancing, if you want to.
如果你想聊聊舞蹈的话。

1112
00:46:57.010 --> 00:47:00.050
I remember when Ken finally was like, okay, cut.
我记得Ken终于喊了“好，卡”。

1113
00:47:00.390 --> 00:47:02.810
Steve was on the ground doing the last worm.
Steve当时正趴在地上做最后一次蠕虫舞。

1114
00:47:02.810 --> 00:47:03.590
Yeah, that was the last one.
对，那是最后一次。

1115
00:47:03.610 --> 00:47:03.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1116
00:47:03.970 --> 00:47:10.870
And he got up and everyone applauded for him and you guys came over and gave him a hug because he had really gone for it.
他站起来时大家都为他鼓掌，你们走过去拥抱了他，因为他真的拼尽全力了。

1117
00:47:10.950 --> 00:47:11.170
That was exhausting.
那太累人了。

1118
00:47:11.350 --> 00:47:12.270
Yeah, he completely did.
没错，他确实拼尽了全力。

1119
00:47:12.410 --> 00:47:13.010
That was amazing.
那太精彩了。

1120
00:47:13.210 --> 00:47:14.430
Here's a fan question.
这里有个粉丝提问。

1121
00:47:14.770 --> 00:47:19.010
Was there music playing when Michael danced or was it added later?
Michael跳舞时有放音乐吗，还是后期加进去的？

1122
00:47:19.810 --> 00:47:22.070
My memory is that it was added later.
我的记忆是后期加进去的。

1123
00:47:22.070 --> 00:47:32.330
I mean, I feel like what we often did was we would do one take with the music and then somebody would have a little earwig, you know, and they would say,
我是说，我觉得我们通常的做法是先跟着音乐拍一次，然后有人会戴个小耳塞，你知道的，他们会说，

1124
00:47:32.430 --> 00:47:33.650
do you want to do it with an earwig?
你想戴着耳塞跳吗？

1125
00:47:33.690 --> 00:47:38.470
And a lot of effort had gone into making a tiny invisible thing that could play the soundtrack.
而且我们花了很多精力去制作一个能播放原声带的微型隐形装置。

1126
00:47:38.730 --> 00:47:40.030
And then the actor would go, no, I don't need it.
然后演员会说，不，我不需要。

1127
00:47:40.790 --> 00:47:44.130
And then it was due to the next five takes just for memory.
接下来的五次拍摄就全靠记忆了。

1128
00:47:44.290 --> 00:47:46.210
That's how I feel like it probably went down.
我觉得当时的情况大概就是这样。

1129
00:47:46.370 --> 00:47:50.190
I do remember some fun facts about the band on Booze Cruise.
我确实记得一些关于“酒水游轮”那集里乐队的趣事。

1130
00:47:50.190 --> 00:47:52.310
Yes, we had a lot of questions about the band.
是的，我们收到了很多关于乐队的问题。

1131
00:47:52.470 --> 00:47:53.410
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

1132
00:47:53.630 --> 00:48:03.770
Because my friend Bob Thiel, Jr., as you were pointing out on your card, who did our theme song, was in the band.
因为正如你卡片上指出的，我的朋友Bob Thiel, Jr.，也就是我们主题曲的创作者，他就在乐队里。

1133
00:48:04.110 --> 00:48:13.750
And three out of the four band people were the guys who played our theme song, Hal Cragen and Dylan also.
乐队四个人里有三个是我们主题曲的演奏者，Hal Cragen和Dylan也在。

1134
00:48:15.090 --> 00:48:18.310
Dylan O'Brien, who's a big songwriter in L.A.
Dylan O'Brien，他是洛杉矶的一位大牌词曲作者。

1135
00:48:18.310 --> 00:48:24.270
And these guys were friends of mine, or Bob was.
这些人都是我的朋友，或者说Bob是我的朋友。

1136
00:48:24.490 --> 00:48:38.030
And the theme song for The Office was written by Jay Ferguson, but he sent over a version of it on Synthesizer, which was, you know, a little – it was great.
《办公室》的主题曲是Jay Ferguson写的，但他发来的是一个合成器版本，你知道的，有点……虽然很棒。

1137
00:48:38.050 --> 00:48:39.130
It was obviously a great song.
那显然是一首很棒的歌。

1138
00:48:39.290 --> 00:48:39.670
Loved it.
我很喜欢。

1139
00:48:39.670 --> 00:48:42.750
But it didn't sound – it didn't have the energy that you'd want.
但听起来……它没有那种你想要的活力。

1140
00:48:43.830 --> 00:48:55.370
And so Bob had this kind of rockin' band that he put together of his friends, and we went and recorded the theme song with all live instruments in a session.
所以Bob找了他的朋友组建了一支摇滚乐队，我们去录音棚用现场乐器录制了主题曲。

1141
00:48:55.730 --> 00:48:55.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1142
00:48:56.190 --> 00:48:57.190
That is so cool.
那太酷了。

1143
00:48:57.190 --> 00:48:58.550
I did not know that.
我之前都不知道。

1144
00:48:58.710 --> 00:48:58.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1145
00:48:59.110 --> 00:49:00.190
That is so cool.
那太酷了。

1146
00:49:00.190 --> 00:49:03.430
And then he became – you know, then he called his band the Scrantones.
后来他把他的乐队命名为“Scrantones”。

1147
00:49:03.730 --> 00:49:03.970
Yeah.
没错。

1148
00:49:04.050 --> 00:49:08.890
And then he came to Scranton with us and would play at our parties often.
后来他跟我们一起去了斯克兰顿，还经常在我们的派对上演奏。

1149
00:49:09.190 --> 00:49:16.410
And he was in the – I had a fan write in and say that he's also in Phyllis' Wedding with Kevin in Scrantonicity.
而且他还在……有粉丝写信说，他在“Phyllis的婚礼”那一集中也和Kevin一起出现在Scrantonicity乐队里。

1150
00:49:16.570 --> 00:49:17.930
I had a fan as well.
我也收到了粉丝的来信。

1151
00:49:18.050 --> 00:49:26.190
Vanessa McLoad said that she noticed that at least one of the band members shows up later in Scrantonicity at Phyllis' Wedding.
凡妮莎·麦克劳德说她注意到至少有一位乐队成员后来出现在了菲利斯的婚礼上，是“斯克兰顿之音”乐队的成员。

1152
00:49:26.250 --> 00:49:27.030
Yeah, it's Bob.
没错，是鲍勃。

1153
00:49:27.030 --> 00:49:33.310
Well, Bob – you know, Bob also did music – the music for Sons of Anarchy and the Mayans.
嗯，鲍勃——你知道，鲍勃还做过音乐——《混乱之子》和《玛雅帮》的音乐。

1154
00:49:33.490 --> 00:49:34.910
So he's quite talented.
所以他很有才华。

1155
00:49:35.090 --> 00:49:35.690
He's so talented.
他太有才了。

1156
00:49:35.950 --> 00:49:36.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1157
00:49:36.000 --> 00:49:38.130
I have it 11 minutes, 14 seconds.
我记的是11分14秒。

1158
00:49:38.410 --> 00:49:39.810
This is really crazy.
这真的很疯狂。

1159
00:49:40.150 --> 00:49:40.200
What?
什么？

1160
00:49:40.200 --> 00:49:41.250
If you know these three people.
如果你认识这三个人。

1161
00:49:41.650 --> 00:49:44.790
Phyllis, Kevin, and Angela are dancing together.
菲利斯、凯文和安吉拉正在一起跳舞。

1162
00:49:45.550 --> 00:49:46.030
Oh.
哦。

1163
00:49:46.230 --> 00:49:46.510
What?
什么？

1164
00:49:47.430 --> 00:49:48.130
I'm telling you.
我跟你说。

1165
00:49:48.130 --> 00:49:52.130
Isn't there a shot of Phyllis dancing with Creed at one point?
是不是有个镜头是菲利斯和克里德在跳舞？

1166
00:49:52.130 --> 00:49:52.510
Yes.
是的。

1167
00:49:52.570 --> 00:49:52.850
Yes.
没错。

1168
00:49:53.110 --> 00:49:54.710
Towards the end, there is.
快结束的时候有。

1169
00:49:54.830 --> 00:49:55.590
They're dancing together.
他们在一起跳舞。

1170
00:49:55.590 --> 00:50:02.710
But we're doing that awkward dance where, like – I almost feel like in eighth grade, we're like a group of girls dance together.
但我们跳的那种尴尬的舞，就像——我感觉就像八年级时，我们一群女生在一起跳舞一样。

1171
00:50:03.150 --> 00:50:04.850
Except it's me, Phyllis, and Kevin.
只不过换成了我和菲利斯还有凯文。

1172
00:50:05.530 --> 00:50:07.990
And we're just kind of doing, like, a little sway like that.
我们只是在那儿晃来晃去。

1173
00:50:08.070 --> 00:50:09.170
It's just very funny to me.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

1174
00:50:09.330 --> 00:50:15.370
Well, I don't know if you remember, Greg, but there was a runner – I read it in the script, and then I went back and I saw it in the deleted scenes.
格雷格，不知道你还记不记得，有个贯穿全集的梗——我在剧本里读到过，后来回去看删减片段时又看到了。

1175
00:50:15.370 --> 00:50:20.550
There was this whole runner through this episode that Oscar is a really mean drunk.
这一集里有个贯穿始终的梗，就是奥斯卡喝醉了之后特别刻薄。

1176
00:50:21.050 --> 00:50:21.450
Yes.
是的。

1177
00:50:21.590 --> 00:50:22.650
I'm glad we cut that.
很高兴我们把它剪掉了。

1178
00:50:23.030 --> 00:50:23.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1179
00:50:23.490 --> 00:50:24.230
I didn't like that.
我不喜欢那个设定。

1180
00:50:24.390 --> 00:50:26.510
I reread the script, too, and I was like, ooh.
我也重读了剧本，当时就觉得，噢。

1181
00:50:26.870 --> 00:50:28.310
Glad we didn't use this.
很高兴我们没用这段。

1182
00:50:28.650 --> 00:50:32.890
Where he's just – he's getting drunk, and then he's going around, and he's insulting all of you.
就是他喝醉了，然后到处去侮辱你们所有人。

1183
00:50:33.010 --> 00:50:35.930
So, that is probably why Oscar is not dancing with you guys.
所以，这可能就是为什么奥斯卡没有和你们一起跳舞。

1184
00:50:36.090 --> 00:50:37.330
And also, later –
而且后来——

1185
00:50:37.330 --> 00:50:38.430
He's isolated himself.
他把自己孤立起来了。

1186
00:50:38.430 --> 00:50:41.750
Yeah, later, it's just Kevin and I in the booth, and that's probably why.
对，后来只有我和凯文在卡座里，可能就是因为这个。

1187
00:50:41.930 --> 00:50:44.410
Because Oscar's off, like, talking about you.
因为奥斯卡跑去说你们坏话了。

1188
00:50:44.590 --> 00:50:45.250
Oh, I forgot about that.
哦，我把这事儿忘了。

1189
00:50:45.350 --> 00:50:50.930
Well, I want to go back to the scene with Jim, Katie, Pam, and Roy sitting around the table.
我想回到吉姆、凯蒂、帕姆和罗伊坐在桌子旁的那场戏。

1190
00:50:51.170 --> 00:50:51.570
Great.
太棒了。

1191
00:50:52.550 --> 00:50:57.070
Katie makes a comment where she says, ah, we're at the cool table.
凯蒂评论说，啊，我们坐在酷桌这边。

1192
00:50:57.630 --> 00:51:01.450
And then they all talk about what they were like in high school, except Jim.
然后除了吉姆，他们都聊了自己高中时是什么样。

1193
00:51:01.450 --> 00:51:09.210
We don't hear about Jim, but we find out that Katie was a cheerleader, and that Pam was artsy-fartsy.
我们没听到吉姆的，但我们发现凯蒂曾是啦啦队长，而帕姆是个文艺青年。

1194
00:51:09.330 --> 00:51:09.990
Thanks, Roy.
谢了，罗伊。

1195
00:51:10.270 --> 00:51:12.430
And that Roy played sports.
还有罗伊是搞体育的。

1196
00:51:12.830 --> 00:51:15.950
And then Amy does her little cheer.
然后艾米跳了她那段小啦啦操。

1197
00:51:16.190 --> 00:51:19.670
Amy, as Katie, does her awesome cheer, and that was not in the script.
艾米，也就是凯蒂，跳了那段精彩的啦啦操，那不在剧本里。

1198
00:51:19.990 --> 00:51:25.070
We found out on the set that Amy Adams was a cheerleader, and she knew a bunch of cheers,
我们在片场发现艾米·亚当斯当过啦啦队长，她会很多啦啦操动作，

1199
00:51:25.290 --> 00:51:29.830
and she did – you had her do little cheers for us to react to.
她做了——你让她为我们表演了几个动作，让我们做出反应。

1200
00:51:29.830 --> 00:51:31.990
So Amy and I did a few cheers together.
所以我和艾米一起跳了几段啦啦操。

1201
00:51:32.470 --> 00:51:34.350
We were all really punchy, you guys.
我们当时都特别亢奋，伙计们。

1202
00:51:34.510 --> 00:51:36.470
It was, like, 3 in the morning, you know?
当时大概是凌晨三点，你们懂的吧？

1203
00:51:36.550 --> 00:51:39.190
So do you remember – because I remember when we were doing that scene,
所以你还记得吗——因为我记得我们在拍那场戏的时候，

1204
00:51:39.670 --> 00:51:44.230
and Amy started to do the cheerleader stuff, we did a couple of takes of it,
艾米开始做啦啦队长的动作，我们拍了好几条，

1205
00:51:44.270 --> 00:51:48.330
and then Ken wanted to move on, and something was bothering me,
然后肯想继续拍下一场，但我心里总觉得有点不对劲，

1206
00:51:48.850 --> 00:51:50.950
and I didn't want to move on from that scene.
我不想就那么跳过那场戏。

1207
00:51:50.950 --> 00:51:55.210
And I realized that the balance – she kind of shifted the balance.
我意识到那种平衡——她打破了某种平衡。

1208
00:51:55.510 --> 00:51:57.450
Because Amy Adams is obviously very charismatic.
因为艾米·亚当斯显然非常有魅力。

1209
00:51:57.810 --> 00:51:57.990
Yeah.
没错。

1210
00:51:58.170 --> 00:51:59.030
You know, beautiful actress.
你知道的，美丽的演员。

1211
00:51:59.030 --> 00:52:05.810
And she did that really fun, cute cheerleader thing, and then we were going to move on.
她做了那个非常有趣、可爱的啦啦队长动作，然后我们就打算继续拍下一场了。

1212
00:52:05.910 --> 00:52:13.290
And I realized, like, Pam is just basically not participating on the same level here.
但我意识到，帕姆基本上没有参与到同样的层面上来。

1213
00:52:13.430 --> 00:52:19.810
She's kind of denying the cheerleader thing, but she isn't doing her own charismatic thing.
她有点在排斥那个啦啦队长的戏份，但她自己又没表现出那种魅力。

1214
00:52:19.890 --> 00:52:23.950
And we went back, and at 9.09, I went back to you, and I said,
于是我们回过头去，在9分09秒的时候，我走到你身边说，

1215
00:52:24.030 --> 00:52:25.110
you've got to kick this up a notch.
你得把劲儿提上来。

1216
00:52:25.190 --> 00:52:26.550
Do you remember that?
你记得吗？

1217
00:52:26.550 --> 00:52:26.850
Yeah.
记得。

1218
00:52:27.010 --> 00:52:31.090
And then you kind of mocked her cheerleader thing, and you did that, and I was like, yeah.
然后你嘲弄了她的啦啦队长动作，你做了那个，我就觉得，对，就是这样。

1219
00:52:31.330 --> 00:52:32.890
Yeah, because that was not in the script.
对，因为剧本里没写那段。

1220
00:52:32.950 --> 00:52:33.570
That wasn't, no.
确实没有，没错。

1221
00:52:33.570 --> 00:52:35.510
That was added in the moment.
那是当时临时加的。

1222
00:52:35.710 --> 00:52:35.890
Yeah.
没错。

1223
00:52:35.930 --> 00:52:40.170
And that's – yeah, I kind of flirt with Jim there.
就是那样——对，我在那儿跟吉姆调情了。

1224
00:52:40.190 --> 00:52:40.330
Yeah.
没错。

1225
00:52:40.330 --> 00:52:40.410
I know.
我知道。

1226
00:52:40.410 --> 00:52:42.190
We have a private moment at the table.
我们在桌边有了私下的互动。

1227
00:52:42.190 --> 00:52:46.130
I thought that was, like, so bold with Roy sitting next to you.
我觉得那真的很大胆，毕竟罗伊当时就坐在你旁边。

1228
00:52:46.250 --> 00:52:52.570
Like, when I watched it again, I was like, wait, she's flirting with Jim, with Roy next
当我重看的时候，我在想，等等，她竟然在罗伊坐在旁边的情况下，

1229
00:52:52.570 --> 00:52:55.390
to her, and also kind of making fun of Katie.
跟吉姆调情，还顺便嘲弄了凯蒂。

1230
00:52:55.530 --> 00:52:55.770
Yeah.
没错。

1231
00:52:55.930 --> 00:52:56.070
Yeah.
对。

1232
00:52:56.070 --> 00:52:57.550
I was like, Pam's having a moment.
我当时心想，帕姆这是有情况啊。

1233
00:52:57.830 --> 00:53:02.510
Well, I think it was an important connection there, Greg, because it is certainly going to
嗯，我觉得那是一个很重要的连接点，格雷格，因为它肯定会

1234
00:53:02.510 --> 00:53:09.730
help give Jim the courage to do what he's going to attempt to do, which is tell Pam his feelings.
帮助吉姆鼓起勇气去做他打算做的事，也就是向帕姆表白他的心意。

1235
00:53:09.990 --> 00:53:10.270
Yeah.
没错。

1236
00:53:10.390 --> 00:53:15.550
I think without that little moment of them bonding over how ridiculous their significant
我觉得如果没有他们在那儿因为另一半的荒唐行为而产生共鸣的小插曲，

1237
00:53:15.550 --> 00:53:20.390
others are being, it's like you need to see them as that bonded couple.
你就没法把他们看作那种心意相通的一对。

1238
00:53:20.870 --> 00:53:21.370
Yeah.
没错。

1239
00:53:21.490 --> 00:53:25.590
So it doesn't come so out of the blue that Jim would think, this could be my moment.
所以吉姆觉得“这可能是我的机会”时，才不会显得那么突兀。

1240
00:53:25.590 --> 00:53:28.810
Well, also, Pam really gives him an opening.
嗯，而且帕姆确实给了他一个机会。

1241
00:53:29.030 --> 00:53:29.530
Yeah.
没错。

1242
00:53:29.530 --> 00:53:30.730
On the top of the boat there.
就在船顶上的时候。

1243
00:53:30.730 --> 00:53:31.270
She does.
她确实给了。

1244
00:53:31.630 --> 00:53:32.130
Yeah.
没错。

1245
00:53:32.430 --> 00:53:38.990
That, to me, the Jim thing of it was she's engaged, and he wants to be a good person and,
对我来说，吉姆那部分的情况是，她已经订婚了，他想做一个好人，

1246
00:53:38.990 --> 00:53:41.170
you know, respect the fact that she's engaged.
你知道的，尊重她已经订婚的事实。

1247
00:53:41.570 --> 00:53:49.310
But he's also, like, there's all these clues coming in that there could be something, and
但他同时也觉得，所有这些迹象都表明他们之间可能有点什么，但

1248
00:53:49.310 --> 00:53:50.490
he doesn't go for it.
他没有采取行动。

1249
00:53:50.570 --> 00:53:54.970
And it's very frustrating to watch.
看着真的很让人抓狂。

1250
00:53:54.970 --> 00:53:55.530
It is.
确实是。

1251
00:53:55.630 --> 00:53:58.730
It's so painful to watch, but also feel so honeSt.
看着真让人揪心，但也感觉非常真实。

1252
00:53:59.030 --> 00:54:00.710
Because that's how you would be.
因为那就是你会有的反应。

1253
00:54:00.870 --> 00:54:04.130
You wouldn't, you'd want to say everything, and you wouldn't be able to.
你不会说出来的，你想把一切都说出来，但你做不到。

1254
00:54:04.430 --> 00:54:13.430
Well, I remember, to me, that was probably one of the most personal and sort of raw things
嗯，我记得对我来说，那可能是我写进剧本里最私人、最原始的东西之一了。

1255
00:54:13.430 --> 00:54:15.630
that I would have put into a script.
我写进剧本里的内容。

1256
00:54:15.630 --> 00:54:25.350
Because it did not feel like a very, like, noble Jim, successful social guy moment.
因为它感觉不像是一个很高尚的吉姆，或者一个成功的社交达人会有的时刻。

1257
00:54:25.350 --> 00:54:30.770
It felt really like, ugh, people are going to hate him for this or disrespect him or whatever.
感觉真的很糟糕，人们会因此讨厌他，或者看不起他之类的。

1258
00:54:30.770 --> 00:54:34.330
So I kind of felt it was risky to put it out there.
所以我当时觉得把它放出来挺冒险的。

1259
00:54:35.750 --> 00:54:36.350
I don't know.
我不知道。

1260
00:54:36.410 --> 00:54:40.330
It was very hard also in the edit to keep it that long.
在剪辑时，要保留那么长的时间也非常困难。

1261
00:54:40.710 --> 00:54:45.690
I mean, we tried to make the same length that you guys really did in the scene.
我是说，我们尽量保持了你们在现场表演时的那种长度。

1262
00:54:45.930 --> 00:54:48.570
And there was a lot of urge to, like, trim that up.
当时真的很有冲动想把它剪短一点。

1263
00:54:48.650 --> 00:54:51.410
That's an awful long time to have people not talk.
让人们沉默那么久，时间太长了。

1264
00:54:51.410 --> 00:54:52.170
Yes.
是的。

1265
00:54:52.410 --> 00:54:53.530
Let's talk about that.
我们来聊聊这个。

1266
00:54:53.810 --> 00:54:54.250
But it's so beautiful.
但它太美了。

1267
00:54:54.530 --> 00:54:55.330
It's so beautiful.
太美了。

1268
00:54:55.710 --> 00:54:57.690
Pam and Jim are on the deck of that boat.
帕姆和吉姆在船的甲板上。

1269
00:54:57.750 --> 00:55:01.170
And Pam does give him an opening.
帕姆确实给了他一个机会。

1270
00:55:01.490 --> 00:55:03.790
She says, sometimes I just don't get Roy.
她说，有时候我就是搞不懂罗伊。

1271
00:55:04.370 --> 00:55:12.490
And this is the first time we've seen her complain about Roy to Jim, to disparage her relationship.
这是我们第一次看到她向吉姆抱怨罗伊，贬低她自己的这段关系。

1272
00:55:13.550 --> 00:55:14.110
Really.
确实。

1273
00:55:14.350 --> 00:55:16.190
It's the first time she's verbalized it.
这是她第一次把它说出口。

1274
00:55:16.270 --> 00:55:17.450
I don't, I'm pretty sure.
我不确定，但我很肯定。

1275
00:55:17.650 --> 00:55:21.050
And then it is 27 seconds of silence.
然后就是长达27秒的沉默。

1276
00:55:21.750 --> 00:55:28.830
And a fan wrote in, Anthony Sneed, said, what was the motivation behind that awkward silence?
有个粉丝安东尼·斯尼德写信问，那段尴尬沉默背后的动机是什么？

1277
00:55:29.150 --> 00:55:31.210
There's a lot going on in those 27 seconds.
那27秒里发生了很多事。

1278
00:55:31.290 --> 00:55:33.810
Just because people aren't talking doesn't mean nothing's going on.
仅仅因为人们没说话，并不代表什么都没发生。

1279
00:55:33.890 --> 00:55:45.710
And I think that you look at his face and, you know, you can see him trying out different things and thinking and being, you know, urged to go forward and blocked and, you know.
我觉得你看他的脸，你知道，你能看到他在尝试不同的想法，在思考，在被某种冲动驱使着前进，又被阻挡，你知道的。

1280
00:55:45.710 --> 00:55:57.510
And then I think also on your face, there's all this kind of like disappointment that he's not going to do anything and face saving when you're like, well, I'm cold.
我觉得在你的脸上，也有那种他什么都不做带来的失望，还有当你说了句“我冷”时那种为了挽回面子的感觉。

1281
00:55:57.710 --> 00:56:00.110
And kind of, it was kind of good that it was cold actually.
而且其实天冷挺好的。

1282
00:56:00.730 --> 00:56:07.910
And we really did shoot it out in the harbor because I think you wouldn't have been able to, like, your nose was red.
我们确实是在港口实景拍摄的，因为我觉得如果不是那样，你的鼻子就不会冻红了。

1283
00:56:08.050 --> 00:56:08.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1284
00:56:08.210 --> 00:56:08.530
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1285
00:56:08.730 --> 00:56:09.730
I was cold.
我是真的很冷。

1286
00:56:09.770 --> 00:56:10.650
Yeah, you were cold.
是啊，你当时确实很冷。

1287
00:56:10.890 --> 00:56:11.910
Yeah, I believed it.
没错，我当时就信了。

1288
00:56:12.030 --> 00:56:14.970
Now, Greg, it wasn't in the script that there would be a big pause.
格雷格，剧本里并没有写会有这么长的停顿。

1289
00:56:15.810 --> 00:56:19.570
It didn't say there's a long, big pause.
上面没写“此处有长长的停顿”。

1290
00:56:19.850 --> 00:56:20.010
Yeah.
是的。

1291
00:56:20.010 --> 00:56:23.770
It just says that they look at each other and then finally Pam says.
上面只写了他们看着对方，然后帕姆终于开口说话了。

1292
00:56:24.390 --> 00:56:24.610
Yeah.
是的。

1293
00:56:25.210 --> 00:56:33.290
But I remember on the day you really encouraging us to take our time and don't be afraid to just look at each other.
但我记得那天你真的鼓励我们慢慢来，不要害怕只是看着对方。

1294
00:56:33.950 --> 00:56:43.490
Well, I mean, that was part of, I think, what made the show so special was that, and so different from what was on TV, you know,
嗯，我是说，我认为这正是让这部剧如此特别的原因，也是它与当时电视上其他节目不同的地方，你知道，

1295
00:56:43.590 --> 00:56:50.710
was that moments of behavior were really important more so than jokes and setups and punchlines and lines and stuff.
行为的瞬间比笑话、铺垫、包袱和台词之类的东西重要得多。

1296
00:56:51.510 --> 00:56:56.650
And so, and I think that came out of appreciating what's good about a documentary,
所以，我认为这源于对纪录片优点的欣赏，

1297
00:56:56.950 --> 00:57:07.990
and documentaries just are all about finding the truth in what people are doing and leaning in and no matter what they think they're doing or what they say they're doing,
纪录片的核心就是发现人们行为背后的真相，深入观察，无论他们自认为在做什么，或者嘴上说在做什么，

1298
00:57:08.710 --> 00:57:11.170
what are their actions show you that they're doing.
他们的行动展现出来的才是他们真正在做的。

1299
00:57:11.170 --> 00:57:21.010
And this was like a good romantic example of, you know, it all being in between the lines and it all being on the faces and not in the script, so.
这是一个很好的浪漫例子，你知道，一切都在字里行间，一切都在脸上，而不是在剧本里，所以。

1300
00:57:21.190 --> 00:57:22.610
That is so smartly said.
说得太精辟了。

1301
00:57:22.750 --> 00:57:26.670
You guys, should we talk about what else was going on during this scene?
伙计们，我们要不要聊聊这场戏拍摄期间还发生了什么？

1302
00:57:27.110 --> 00:57:30.090
Do you mean when half of the cast got lost at sea?
你是说有一半演员在海上失踪那次吗？

1303
00:57:30.650 --> 00:57:31.090
Yes.
没错。

1304
00:57:32.590 --> 00:57:34.230
All right, so here's the deal.
好吧，情况是这样的。

1305
00:57:34.470 --> 00:57:37.590
When we started this scene, I think we knew it was going to take a while.
开始拍这场戏的时候，我想我们都知道这会花不少时间。

1306
00:57:37.590 --> 00:57:47.490
Well, and so they told the other cast members that they could leave for the day, but the only way to get off the boat, because we weren't going to take the boat back and dock it.
嗯，所以他们告诉其他演员可以先收工了，但离开船的唯一方式，因为我们当时不会把大船开回去靠岸。

1307
00:57:47.590 --> 00:57:52.870
No, there were these little dinghies that would pull up, and you would get in the little boat, and it would take you to shore.
不，当时有那种小橡皮艇会靠过来，你得坐进小船里，它会把你送回岸上。

1308
00:57:53.010 --> 00:57:53.410
Exactly.
没错。

1309
00:57:54.110 --> 00:57:56.350
Well, that did not go as planned.
结果，事情没按计划进行。

1310
00:57:56.730 --> 00:57:57.770
No, it didn't.
确实没有。

1311
00:57:57.870 --> 00:58:00.750
I remember getting this panicky radio thing.
我记得当时收到了一个惊慌失措的无线电消息。

1312
00:58:01.210 --> 00:58:03.490
The boat with Phyllis on it is gone.
载着菲利斯的船不见了。

1313
00:58:03.830 --> 00:58:05.470
Look, look, look at my card.
看，看，看我的卡片。

1314
00:58:05.630 --> 00:58:06.450
You were on the boat too.
你当时也在那艘船上。

1315
00:58:06.450 --> 00:58:07.930
I was stranded on the boat.
我被困在那艘船上了。

1316
00:58:08.130 --> 00:58:09.790
Yeah, and Brian too, right?
对，还有布莱恩，对吧？

1317
00:58:09.890 --> 00:58:12.490
And Rain, and I wrote about it in my journal.
还有雷恩，我在日记里写过这件事。

1318
00:58:12.710 --> 00:58:12.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1319
00:58:13.590 --> 00:58:14.450
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

1320
00:58:14.630 --> 00:58:17.430
Well, for some reason, it fixated on me that it was Phyllis.
嗯，不知道为什么，我当时认定失踪的是菲利斯。

1321
00:58:17.570 --> 00:58:19.870
That Phyllis was, that we had lost Phyllis.
认定菲利斯，我们把菲利斯弄丢了。

1322
00:58:19.870 --> 00:58:22.230
She seems like the most vulnerable of the group.
她看起来是这群人里最脆弱的一个。

1323
00:58:22.370 --> 00:58:22.530
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1324
00:58:22.530 --> 00:58:23.630
Right, kind Phyllis.
没错，善良的菲利斯。

1325
00:58:23.690 --> 00:58:27.210
Yeah, so I wrote her about it, and she-
对，所以我写信问她这件事，然后她——

1326
00:58:27.210 --> 00:58:28.330
I can't wait to hear what she says.
真想听听她怎么说。

1327
00:58:28.330 --> 00:58:35.350
Yeah, well, she says the first memory, she said it was about 2.30 in the morning, and she was waiting to leave the ship,
嗯，她说她第一个记忆是大约凌晨两点半，她当时正等着离开大船，

1328
00:58:35.350 --> 00:58:43.730
and her first memory was seeing Steve Carell on a tiny little boat, holding onto some kind of a pole with no life jacket, disappearing into the night.
她第一个记忆是看到史蒂夫·卡瑞尔坐在一艘极小的船上，手里抓着一根杆子，没穿救生衣，消失在夜色中。

1329
00:58:43.730 --> 00:58:53.510
And she remembers thinking that if NBC knew that their star was just, didn't have a life jacket and was, you know, being pulled off back to the harbor, they would be upset.
她记得当时心想，如果NBC知道他们的当家明星没穿救生衣，就这样被拉回港口，他们肯定会气疯的。

1330
00:58:53.510 --> 00:59:02.510
And then she got on the boat, and she thought it was Oscar, Brian, and somebody from the wardrobe department.
然后她上了船，她以为船上还有奥斯卡、布莱恩，以及服装组的某个人。

1331
00:59:03.390 --> 00:59:05.290
I wrote about it the day of.
我当天就写了这件事。

1332
00:59:05.330 --> 00:59:05.510
But that was you.
但那个人是你。

1333
00:59:05.750 --> 00:59:05.910
Yeah.
没错。

1334
00:59:06.290 --> 00:59:08.090
No, she says, I'm not sure if Angela was there or not.
不，她说，我不确定安吉拉当时在不在。

1335
00:59:08.450 --> 00:59:11.210
And then she talks, everything was fine pulling away.
然后她说，刚开走的时候一切正常。

1336
00:59:11.370 --> 00:59:16.590
We were enjoying the smell of the ocean, the lights in the distance, and then all of a sudden, nothing.
我们正享受着海风的味道，看着远处的灯光，突然之间，什么都没了。

1337
00:59:16.590 --> 00:59:17.610
The engine died.
引擎熄火了。

1338
00:59:18.230 --> 00:59:19.190
So you were there.
所以你当时也在场。

1339
00:59:19.190 --> 00:59:24.390
So this is what I wrote the day after we filmed the scene.
这是我拍完那场戏的第二天写的。

1340
00:59:24.750 --> 00:59:25.190
All right.
好吧。

1341
00:59:25.310 --> 00:59:31.430
I wrote, one of the coolest things that happened to me while we shot this episode happened the last night, or I guess I should say the morning of.
我写道，拍摄这一集期间发生的最酷的事情之一发生在最后一晚，或者我应该说是凌晨。

1342
00:59:31.590 --> 00:59:35.050
Rain, Phyllis, and Brian and I were all wrapped at 5.30 a.m.
雷恩、菲利斯、布莱恩和我都在凌晨5点半收工了。

1343
00:59:35.430 --> 00:59:42.470
We were on the main boat, but they said they had more shooting to do so we could stay on the big boat and, like, sleep in a booth.
我们当时在大船上，但他们说还有戏要拍，所以我们可以留在船上，比如在卡座里睡一觉。

1344
00:59:43.050 --> 00:59:43.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1345
00:59:43.290 --> 00:59:49.670
Or they said they had these little rubber boats that would pull up next to the big boat that we could get on and they would take us to shore.
或者他们说有那种小橡皮艇会靠在大船旁边，我们可以坐上去，他们会把我们送回岸上。

1346
00:59:50.290 --> 00:59:52.050
So we said, okay, we'll do that.
于是我们说，好吧，就这么办。

1347
00:59:52.130 --> 00:59:55.290
They said it's about a 15-minute boat ride on the little rubber dinghy.
他们说坐这种小橡皮艇回岸上大约需要15分钟。

1348
00:59:56.230 --> 00:59:57.390
So we decided to do it.
所以我们决定这么做。

1349
00:59:57.510 --> 00:59:59.630
It was really tricky getting on the rubber boat.
上那艘橡皮艇真的挺费劲的。

1350
00:59:59.810 --> 01:00:00.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1351
01:00:00.290 --> 01:00:03.430
We just had to climb out a ladder off the side of the boat.
我们当时不得不从船侧爬梯子下去。

1352
01:00:03.850 --> 01:00:04.530
And these guys kind of-
然后这些人有点……

1353
01:00:04.530 --> 01:00:05.090
It was very unstable.
那船非常不稳定。

1354
01:00:05.390 --> 01:00:05.610
Very-
非常……

1355
01:00:05.610 --> 01:00:07.750
Phyllis said that at one point she had to switch boats.
菲利斯说有一次她不得不换船。

1356
01:00:07.750 --> 01:00:09.430
She was terrified of falling in.
她当时怕得要命，生怕掉进水里。

1357
01:00:09.430 --> 01:00:09.870
Yes.
是的。

1358
01:00:10.030 --> 01:00:21.110
And I said, okay, the little rubber boat, picture the kind of, like, rubber boat that the Navy SEALs do the backflips off of with the little, like, outboat.
我说，好吧，就是那种小橡皮艇，想象一下海豹突击队那种会向后翻入水中的橡皮艇，带个小舷外马达的那种。

1359
01:00:21.210 --> 01:00:22.130
That's what this looked like.
看起来就是那样的。

1360
01:00:22.430 --> 01:00:29.810
So we're lowered down into it, and it was me, Rain, Jen, one of our wardrobe gals, Phyllis, and Brian.
于是我们被放了下去，船上有我、雷恩、珍、我们的一位服装师、菲利斯，还有布莱恩。

1361
01:00:30.090 --> 01:00:31.970
It was tiny and really bouncy.
船很小，而且晃得厉害。

1362
01:00:31.970 --> 01:00:32.710
We took off.
我们出发了。

1363
01:00:32.770 --> 01:00:35.550
It was dark out, and the ocean looked like black glass.
外面天很黑，海面看起来像黑色的玻璃。

1364
01:00:35.730 --> 01:00:36.870
It was very peaceful.
非常宁静。

1365
01:00:37.170 --> 01:00:38.330
Oh, it's so poetic.
哦，太有诗意了。

1366
01:00:38.330 --> 01:00:38.830
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1367
01:00:39.050 --> 01:00:39.530
Sorry.
抱歉。

1368
01:00:40.030 --> 01:00:45.130
About five minutes into our ride, our engine made a weird whirring sound and stopped working.
行驶了大约五分钟后，引擎发出奇怪的呼呼声，然后就停转了。

1369
01:00:45.810 --> 01:00:49.710
And then we heard the boat driver radio and say, the engine's dead.
接着我们听到船夫用无线电说，引擎坏了。

1370
01:00:49.710 --> 01:00:50.990
You need to come get us.
你们得过来接我们。

1371
01:00:51.310 --> 01:00:54.270
Brian started laughing and said, you've got to be kidding me.
布莱恩开始大笑，说，你一定是在开玩笑吧。

1372
01:00:54.970 --> 01:00:58.610
Then we just floated in the darkness, which felt like for a while.
然后我们就漂浮在黑暗中，感觉过了好久。

1373
01:00:59.310 --> 01:01:01.510
It was quiet and peaceful.
当时很安静，很平和。

1374
01:01:01.750 --> 01:01:02.790
It turned into the Titanic.
结果变成了泰坦尼克号现场。

1375
01:01:03.070 --> 01:01:03.550
I know.
我知道。

1376
01:01:03.730 --> 01:01:04.390
I know.
我知道。

1377
01:01:04.390 --> 01:01:13.370
Oh, and then we, another rubber boat pulled up, and then we had to just straddle from one rubber boat with just two guys kind of holding it together into the other one.
哦，然后我们，另一艘橡皮艇靠了过来，我们不得不跨过去，全靠两个人在中间勉强扶着两艘船。

1378
01:01:13.510 --> 01:01:14.650
This was very tricky.
这非常棘手。

1379
01:01:15.210 --> 01:01:17.430
We slowly made our way past the Queen Mary.
我们慢慢地经过了玛丽皇后号。

1380
01:01:17.630 --> 01:01:24.890
Picture an old cruise ship that looks like the Titanic, and there was a huge plume of fire coming from a refinery behind it.
想象一艘看起来像泰坦尼克号的老式游轮，后面炼油厂冒出巨大的火柱。

1381
01:01:25.270 --> 01:01:27.270
Rain said to me, this is so surreal.
雷恩对我说，这太超现实了。

1382
01:01:27.810 --> 01:01:29.570
And that's exactly what it was.
事实确实如此。

1383
01:01:29.790 --> 01:01:32.930
You know, the wheels really came off when we went on locations.
你知道，我们去外景地拍摄时，情况真的失控了。

1384
01:01:33.190 --> 01:01:34.730
We talk about this a little bit.
我们稍微聊过这个。

1385
01:01:34.730 --> 01:01:39.890
I mean, you know, this is for season nine, but, you know, death bus almost killed us all.
我是说，你知道，这是第九季的事，但那辆“死亡巴士”差点害死我们所有人。

1386
01:01:40.270 --> 01:01:40.550
Yes.
是的。

1387
01:01:40.690 --> 01:01:41.210
Work bus.
工作巴士。

1388
01:01:41.310 --> 01:01:41.570
Work bus.
工作巴士。

1389
01:01:41.610 --> 01:01:42.150
I should say.
我应该这么说。

1390
01:01:42.590 --> 01:01:44.630
We've called it death bus for so long.
我们叫它“死亡巴士”太久了。

1391
01:01:44.770 --> 01:01:46.170
The cast calls it death bus.
演员们都叫它“死亡巴士”。

1392
01:01:46.450 --> 01:01:46.970
All right.
好吧。

1393
01:01:47.050 --> 01:01:48.430
Well, we'll take a break, and we'll be back.
那么，我们先休息一下，马上回来。

1394
01:01:48.650 --> 01:01:53.680
All right.
好的。

1395
01:01:53.680 --> 01:01:54.860
So we are back from break.
我们休息回来了。

1396
01:01:55.560 --> 01:01:57.500
I have a question for you, Greg.
格雷格，我有个问题想问你。

1397
01:01:57.660 --> 01:01:57.780
Yeah.
说吧。

1398
01:01:57.920 --> 01:01:59.560
I've been waiting to ask you this.
我一直等着问你这个。

1399
01:01:59.560 --> 01:02:09.800
I know we're sort of jumping around with time codes, but at 11 minutes, 34 seconds, there's this beautiful shot that goes outside of the boat and goes around the boat.
我知道我们的时间码有点跳跃，但在11分34秒的时候，有一个很美的镜头，从船内拍到船外，绕着船转了一圈。

1400
01:02:09.960 --> 01:02:14.340
You pass Dwight, right, like steering, and it goes around the boat.
你经过了正在掌舵的德怀特，然后镜头绕过了船。

1401
01:02:14.420 --> 01:02:15.280
How did we do that?
我们是怎么做到的？

1402
01:02:15.760 --> 01:02:17.120
That is Kent Zabornak.
那是肯特·扎博纳克。

1403
01:02:17.520 --> 01:02:28.940
So Kent was our line producer, and he was also in the DGA, and, you know, he managed to launch us on the budget that we had, which was tiny.
肯特是我们的制片主任，他也是美国导演工会成员，你知道，他设法让我们在极其有限的预算下完成了拍摄。

1404
01:02:29.560 --> 01:02:39.680
You know, into Long Beach Harbor on a boat for days and get hotel rooms for everybody, and he realized that we really needed a shot like that.
你知道，他让我们在长滩港的船上待了好几天，还给所有人安排了酒店房间，他意识到我们确实需要那样的镜头。

1405
01:02:39.840 --> 01:02:45.000
And he shot that himself with his own equipment, you know,
于是他用自己的设备亲自拍了那个镜头，你知道的，

1406
01:02:45.160 --> 01:02:53.360
while we were shooting the rest of it because he just had an instinct that there was no way the production could get that and stop everything.
就在我们拍摄其他部分的时候，因为他有一种直觉，觉得剧组不可能专门为了那个镜头而停下所有工作。

1407
01:02:53.660 --> 01:02:57.960
And, you know, so that was kind of a guerrilla move and super valuable.
所以，那算是一种游击式的拍摄手法，非常有价值。

1408
01:02:58.640 --> 01:03:01.980
And Kent was, you know, fantastic at doing those kind of things.
肯特在处理这类事情上一直都很棒。

1409
01:03:02.180 --> 01:03:07.520
Like, he was always stitching together amazing stuff on our little budget.
他总能在我们那点微薄的预算下，拼凑出令人惊叹的内容。

1410
01:03:08.100 --> 01:03:09.100
That is so cool.
太酷了。

1411
01:03:09.220 --> 01:03:09.980
I did not know that.
我之前都不知道。

1412
01:03:10.100 --> 01:03:10.300
Did you?
你知道吗？

1413
01:03:10.460 --> 01:03:10.640
No.
不知道。

1414
01:03:10.640 --> 01:03:16.300
Like, when I saw it, I was like, wait, I know Randall and Matt were inside with us.
当我看到那个镜头时，我在想，等等，我知道兰德尔和马特当时和我们在一起。

1415
01:03:16.300 --> 01:03:17.000
Yeah, who did that, right?
是啊，那是谁拍的，对吧？

1416
01:03:17.000 --> 01:03:17.680
Our camera guys.
我们的摄影师。

1417
01:03:17.700 --> 01:03:18.800
I was like, how did that happen?
我当时就在想，那是怎么拍出来的？

1418
01:03:18.800 --> 01:03:20.880
And then I was like, is that a plane?
然后我又想，那是飞机吗？

1419
01:03:20.880 --> 01:03:22.740
I mean, like, it's in the air.
我的意思是，它在空中。

1420
01:03:22.940 --> 01:03:23.320
Like, how?
怎么做到的？

1421
01:03:23.520 --> 01:03:24.820
That, I mean, is it a drone?
那是，我是说，那是无人机吗？

1422
01:03:24.960 --> 01:03:25.700
Like, what is it?
那到底是什么？

1423
01:03:25.720 --> 01:03:26.860
He's on one of those dinghies.
他当时在那种小艇上。

1424
01:03:27.220 --> 01:03:28.960
He's on one of those Zodiac dinghies.
他当时在那种橡皮艇上。

1425
01:03:29.000 --> 01:03:29.100
Oh, he's on a dinghy.
哦，他在小艇上啊。

1426
01:03:29.120 --> 01:03:29.260
Yeah.
是的。

1427
01:03:29.400 --> 01:03:29.640
Okay.
好吧。

1428
01:03:30.020 --> 01:03:30.180
Yeah.
是的。

1429
01:03:30.400 --> 01:03:30.760
All right.
行吧。

1430
01:03:30.920 --> 01:03:31.200
Wow.
哇。

1431
01:03:31.420 --> 01:03:35.060
This is another question about a camera movement.
这是另一个关于运镜的问题。

1432
01:03:35.060 --> 01:03:46.280
So, you know, after they're at the bar and they're all talking about who they would save, Jim gets up his courage and he's going to walk over to Pam and he says,
在他们去酒吧谈论要救谁之后，吉姆鼓起勇气准备走向帕姆，他说，

1433
01:03:46.440 --> 01:03:47.820
I would save the receptioniSt.
我会救前台接待员。

1434
01:03:47.920 --> 01:03:49.240
I think I need to make that clear.
我觉得我有必要把这一点说清楚。

1435
01:03:49.540 --> 01:03:53.960
Well, right before that, Greg Phelps noticed at 14 minutes, 37 seconds,
嗯，就在那之前，格雷格·菲尔普斯注意到在14分37秒时，

1436
01:03:54.120 --> 01:04:00.340
there's a continuous shot of Jim looking down the length of the boat to Pam as he thinks about who he would save.
有一个连续镜头，吉姆沿着船身看向帕姆，当时他正在思考要救谁。

1437
01:04:00.340 --> 01:04:05.740
The camera then zooms in on Pam at the exact moment she has a really cute laughing smile.
镜头随后推向帕姆，正好捕捉到她露出非常可爱笑容的那一刻。

1438
01:04:06.180 --> 01:04:08.200
How did you time that out so perfectly?
你们是怎么把时间掐得那么准的？

1439
01:04:09.000 --> 01:04:13.280
He wants to know, Jenna, were you given a cue when the camera was about to zoom in on you?
他想知道，珍娜，当镜头要推向你时，有人给你提示吗？

1440
01:04:13.400 --> 01:04:15.500
But we used to do that stuff all the time.
但我们以前经常那样做。

1441
01:04:16.540 --> 01:04:17.720
That was, go ahead.
那是，你请说。

1442
01:04:17.720 --> 01:04:29.700
People, I think, have the wrong idea about how we did the show in a way because, like, most filmmaking is super intentional and you would say to the camera operator, okay,
我觉得人们对我们拍摄这部剧的方式可能有些误解，因为大多数电影制作是非常刻意的，你会对摄影师说，好的，

1443
01:04:30.040 --> 01:04:36.300
at this signal you need to zoom in and then you'd try and get the actor to do it at exactly the right time.
在收到信号时你需要推镜头，然后你会尽量让演员在恰当的时间配合。

1444
01:04:36.300 --> 01:04:42.440
And our show was more like the theory of natural selection, kind of, like,
而我们的剧更像是自然选择理论，就像是，

1445
01:04:42.440 --> 01:04:54.100
there would be a situation and I would give notes or the directors would give notes to the camera operators that were not about what they did specifically but more about their intentions.
会出现某种情况，我会或者导演会给摄影师一些建议，不是关于他们具体该怎么做，而是关于他们的拍摄意图。

1446
01:04:54.100 --> 01:05:01.880
So we would say, okay, you're really interested in what he sees down at the end of the hall, so just go find it.
所以我们会说，好的，你现在对走廊尽头他看到的东西很感兴趣，那就去把它找出来。

1447
01:05:02.120 --> 01:05:08.680
And we had all these people who'd come from reality shows who were used to finding the story on their own.
我们有很多来自真人秀的工作人员，他们习惯于自己去寻找故事。

1448
01:05:09.880 --> 01:05:12.500
And that turned out great, you know.
结果证明这非常棒。

1449
01:05:12.740 --> 01:05:15.620
And I can't really speak for Ken as the director.
至于肯作为导演的想法，我不能替他发言。

1450
01:05:15.800 --> 01:05:21.020
He directed it and he might have known exactly what he was going for and kept doing it until he got it.
是他执导的，他可能非常清楚自己想要什么，并一直拍到满意为止。

1451
01:05:21.020 --> 01:05:29.900
But a lot of the times there were just lots of happy accidents and then you'd tell the story through all the happy accidents and you had enough, like,
但很多时候，会有许多意外的惊喜，然后你就可以通过这些意外的惊喜来讲述故事，而且你拥有足够的，比如，

1452
01:05:30.300 --> 01:05:34.100
flexibility that you could have gone a bunch of different ways with it.
灵活性，让你能以多种不同的方式去处理它。

1453
01:05:34.280 --> 01:05:36.400
I think our editors don't get enough credit.
我觉得我们的剪辑师得到的赞誉还不够多。

1454
01:05:36.560 --> 01:05:42.700
Well, first of all, I think our camera operators don't get enough credit for all of those happy accidents.
嗯，首先，我觉得我们的摄影师在促成那些意外惊喜方面，得到的赞誉也不够多。

1455
01:05:42.880 --> 01:05:49.760
But then you would assemble those with the editors in the editing room to tell even more of a story than what was in the script.
但随后你会和剪辑师在剪辑室里把这些素材拼凑起来，讲述一个比剧本里更丰富的故事。

1456
01:05:51.020 --> 01:05:51.460
Totally.
完全同意。

1457
01:05:51.720 --> 01:05:53.120
The editors are amazing.
剪辑师们太棒了。

1458
01:05:53.420 --> 01:05:54.800
We had fantastic editors.
我们有非常出色的剪辑师。

1459
01:05:55.200 --> 01:05:56.060
This one was Dean.
其中一位是迪恩。

1460
01:05:57.120 --> 01:06:01.720
Dave Rogers, as you know, I'm still working with, work with him all the time.
戴夫·罗杰斯，如你所知，我至今仍在和他合作，一直都在一起工作。

1461
01:06:01.960 --> 01:06:02.160
Brilliant.
才华横溢。

1462
01:06:03.880 --> 01:06:04.780
Claire Scanlon.
克莱尔·斯坎伦。

1463
01:06:04.780 --> 01:06:05.560
Claire Scanlon.
克莱尔·斯坎伦。

1464
01:06:05.760 --> 01:06:06.360
Also brilliant.
同样才华横溢。

1465
01:06:08.360 --> 01:06:21.340
And there was enormous amounts of leeway for the editors and in post because like a documentary, we shot way more stuff than we could ever possibly use.
而且剪辑师和后期制作有巨大的发挥空间，因为就像拍纪录片一样，我们拍摄的素材远多于我们实际能用到的。

1466
01:06:21.480 --> 01:06:29.780
And so our rough cuts were always about 38 minutes long, but the show's only 21 minutes, you know, six seconds or something like that.
所以我们的粗剪版通常有38分钟长，但节目只有21分零6秒左右，你知道的。

1467
01:06:29.780 --> 01:06:33.220
So tons of good material was discarded.
因此，大量的优质素材被舍弃了。

1468
01:06:34.600 --> 01:06:37.740
And that was like a large part of my job.
那也是我工作中的很大一部分。

1469
01:06:37.880 --> 01:06:42.400
Like I loved being on set, you know, and I also loved being with the writers.
我喜欢在片场，你知道，我也喜欢和编剧们在一起。

1470
01:06:42.660 --> 01:06:51.460
But this whole other area of my job was sitting with the editors and, you know, and they're fun people too with great, you know, creative ideas.
但我工作的另一大块内容是和剪辑师坐在一起，他们也是很有趣的人，有很多很棒的创意。

1471
01:06:51.460 --> 01:06:57.740
And you could tell so many different versions of the show by what you left in and what you took out.
你可以通过保留和删减不同的内容，来讲述出许多不同版本的节目。

1472
01:06:58.200 --> 01:07:06.180
And like there was, and there was always a thing where you'd like, you'd go, everybody kind of agreed on the first six or eight minutes to get rid of, you know.
而且总会有那么一种情况，大家都会达成共识，觉得前六到八分钟的内容可以删掉。

1473
01:07:06.360 --> 01:07:14.040
And like it probably, we all agreed like having Oscar make snarky mean comments is not great, you know, or whatever it is.
比如我们可能都同意，让奥斯卡发表刻薄的评论并不好，诸如此类的。

1474
01:07:14.140 --> 01:07:17.960
But then you'd get to like about 26 minutes and there was a lot of really good stuff.
但当你剪到26分钟左右时，会有很多非常好的内容。

1475
01:07:18.140 --> 01:07:23.540
And I used to have all these regrets about things that were great that couldn't get in the show.
我过去常常为那些没能放进节目里的精彩片段感到遗憾。

1476
01:07:23.540 --> 01:07:31.360
So one of them for this, if you remember, was Creed sitting in with the band and us finding out that he'd been in the grassroots.
所以其中一个例子，如果你还记得的话，就是克里德加入乐队，我们发现他曾经是“草根乐队”成员的那段。

1477
01:07:31.660 --> 01:07:31.980
Yeah.
没错。

1478
01:07:32.400 --> 01:07:34.420
And that was like fantastic.
那段真是太棒了。

1479
01:07:34.420 --> 01:07:47.100
And we had all this footage and I found footage of him from, you know, late 60s and, you know, playing guitar with the grassroots on Playboy After Dark with Hugh Hefner.
我们有所有的这些素材，我甚至找到了他60年代末的影像，你知道，他在休·海夫纳的《花花公子深夜秀》上和“草根乐队”一起弹吉他。

1480
01:07:47.100 --> 01:07:57.240
Like all this great footage, which was going to be the B-roll under the, you know, under him talking about playing with all these greats in the late 60s.
全是这些很棒的素材，原本打算作为他讲述60年代末与那些大人物一起演奏时的背景画面。

1481
01:07:57.320 --> 01:07:58.660
And that was in for a really long time.
那段内容保留了很长一段时间。

1482
01:07:58.700 --> 01:08:00.220
I think it's in the DVD extras.
我想它在DVD的花絮里。

1483
01:08:00.520 --> 01:08:00.860
It is.
确实在。

1484
01:08:00.900 --> 01:08:01.920
It's in the deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

1485
01:08:02.020 --> 01:08:02.520
It's great.
那段很棒。

1486
01:08:02.760 --> 01:08:08.440
Michael, the guitar player is going to take a break and then Michael tries to fill in for him and he's horrible.
迈克尔，吉他手要休息一下，然后迈克尔试着替补上场，结果他弹得太烂了。

1487
01:08:08.700 --> 01:08:10.700
And then Creed says, let me give it a shot.
然后克里德说，让我来试试。

1488
01:08:10.900 --> 01:08:13.600
And then he just gets up there and rocks out.
接着他走上去，弹得非常带劲。

1489
01:08:13.740 --> 01:08:15.720
And it's so cool and satisfying.
那段真的很酷，让人很满足。

1490
01:08:15.720 --> 01:08:19.900
And then he has a talking head where he explains that he is himself, basically.
然后他有一个采访镜头，解释说他基本上就是在做他自己。

1491
01:08:20.200 --> 01:08:20.460
Yeah.
没错。

1492
01:08:20.500 --> 01:08:23.140
That he is Creed Breton, a member of Grassroots.
说他就是克里德·布雷顿，曾经是“草根乐队”的成员。

1493
01:08:23.380 --> 01:08:23.540
Yeah.
没错。

1494
01:08:23.740 --> 01:08:26.100
And that he kind of fried his brain with drug use.
而且他因为吸毒把脑子搞坏了。

1495
01:08:26.180 --> 01:08:26.340
Yeah.
没错。

1496
01:08:26.340 --> 01:08:28.940
And now he can barely concentrate on his job.
现在他几乎无法集中精力工作。

1497
01:08:29.580 --> 01:08:33.640
And then there's a talking head of Angela going, he wasn't that good or something like that.
然后还有安吉拉的采访镜头，她说，他弹得也没那么好之类的。

1498
01:08:34.760 --> 01:08:35.580
I've seen better.
我见过弹得更好的。

1499
01:08:36.100 --> 01:08:36.900
Oh, man.
天哪。

1500
01:08:37.080 --> 01:08:40.540
By the way, I would wear a shirt that says, I'd save the receptioniSt.
顺便说一句，我会穿一件印着“我会救前台”字样的T恤。

1501
01:08:40.700 --> 01:08:41.220
I think that is-
我觉得那是——

1502
01:08:41.220 --> 01:08:44.220
We should have shirts that say, I'd save the receptioniSt.
我们应该做些T恤，上面写着“我会拯救前台接待员”。

1503
01:08:44.360 --> 01:08:45.160
I think that's so cute.
我觉得那太可爱了。

1504
01:08:45.160 --> 01:08:49.440
I think Ken did a really good job with that, too, because that was, I believe, supposed to just be a talking head.
我觉得肯（Ken）在那方面也做得非常好，因为我记得那本来应该只是一个访谈片段。

1505
01:08:50.180 --> 01:08:50.860
And he-
而且他——

1506
01:08:50.860 --> 01:08:52.240
Yes, in the script, it's a talking head.
是的，剧本里写的就是一个访谈片段。

1507
01:08:52.240 --> 01:08:52.420
Yeah.
没错。

1508
01:08:52.700 --> 01:08:57.420
And he really rightly said, well, where exactly did he say this?
他非常敏锐地提出，他到底是在哪里说的这些话呢？

1509
01:08:57.420 --> 01:09:06.000
Because he had the thought, and then he walks over to Pam, and then she gets interrupted by Roy setting a date.
因为他有了那个想法，然后他走向帕姆（Pam），接着罗伊（Roy）打断了她，说要定个日期。

1510
01:09:06.000 --> 01:09:11.020
So he couldn't figure out where there was going to be a time to interview him about this.
所以他想不出什么时候能有机会就这件事采访他。

1511
01:09:11.120 --> 01:09:16.620
And so he sort of invented this on-the-fly interview where he kind of just passed the cameraman and set it into camera.
于是他临时想出了这个访谈方式，他路过摄影师时顺便对着镜头说了出来。

1512
01:09:16.620 --> 01:09:18.620
And then it was cool.
结果效果很棒。

1513
01:09:19.440 --> 01:09:19.660
Yeah.
是啊。

1514
01:09:19.740 --> 01:09:20.040
Very cool.
非常棒。

1515
01:09:20.040 --> 01:09:20.880
No, I really liked that.
不，我真的很喜欢那个处理。

1516
01:09:21.080 --> 01:09:22.180
No, and you're with him.
没错，而且你会站在他那边。

1517
01:09:22.380 --> 01:09:23.460
Like, Jim's got his courage.
就像是，吉姆（Jim）终于鼓起了勇气。

1518
01:09:23.520 --> 01:09:25.260
He's going to save the receptioniSt.
他要去拯救前台接待员了。

1519
01:09:25.440 --> 01:09:33.100
He almost gets up to Pam, and that's when Roy stands up and says that he's setting a wedding date, June 10th.
他差点就走到帕姆身边了，就在这时罗伊站起来说他要定结婚日期，6月10号。

1520
01:09:33.100 --> 01:09:41.300
A fan question from Ed's Arquiza said, was Pam genuinely happy when Roy proposed, or was she just caught up in the moment?
一位粉丝Ed Arquiza提问说，罗伊求婚时帕姆是真的开心，还是只是被当时的气氛感染了？

1521
01:09:41.580 --> 01:09:42.940
Well, I looked at the script.
嗯，我看了剧本。

1522
01:09:43.180 --> 01:09:45.700
The script said, Pam looks happy.
剧本上写着，帕姆看起来很开心。

1523
01:09:46.000 --> 01:09:52.080
So I played it that Pam was genuinely kind of overcome with this moment.
所以我演的时候，表现出帕姆确实被那一刻深深打动了。

1524
01:09:52.380 --> 01:09:54.680
You know, she's been trying to get Roy's attention.
你知道，她一直试图引起罗伊的注意。

1525
01:09:54.680 --> 01:09:58.740
I think she wants him to treat her like this so badly.
我觉得她太渴望他能这样对待她了。

1526
01:09:59.580 --> 01:10:00.660
And so-
所以——

1527
01:10:00.660 --> 01:10:03.080
She's also invested years into this relationship.
她也在这段感情里投入了多年。

1528
01:10:03.080 --> 01:10:03.700
I know.
我知道。

1529
01:10:03.700 --> 01:10:08.840
And I feel for her because she's like, all right, we're going to do it.
我为她感到难过，因为她当时想的是，好吧，我们要成了。

1530
01:10:08.980 --> 01:10:09.620
This is it.
就是现在了。

1531
01:10:09.840 --> 01:10:10.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1532
01:10:10.220 --> 01:10:14.380
I think it makes it so much worse, too, because he had his moment on the deck.
我觉得这让情况变得更糟了，因为他在甲板上本来有过机会的。

1533
01:10:14.520 --> 01:10:14.820
Yeah.
没错。

1534
01:10:15.040 --> 01:10:18.300
And she was quite receptive there, and then he didn't go for anything.
当时她反应挺积极的，但他什么都没做。

1535
01:10:18.540 --> 01:10:25.200
And then here, look how happy she is that she, you know, finally, after three years of being, you know, strung along.
而现在，你看她有多开心，你知道的，在被吊了三年胃口之后，终于等到了。

1536
01:10:25.660 --> 01:10:25.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1537
01:10:33.080 --> 01:10:33.300
You know?
你懂吗？

1538
01:10:33.500 --> 01:10:33.740
Yeah.
嗯。

1539
01:10:33.900 --> 01:10:34.240
Yes.
是的。

1540
01:10:34.300 --> 01:10:34.980
It's heartbreaking.
这太令人心碎了。

1541
01:10:35.280 --> 01:10:37.020
And then he's mean to Katie.
然后他对凯蒂（Katie）又很刻薄。

1542
01:10:37.520 --> 01:10:40.760
Well, Amy's, first of all, Amy's reaction is so sweet.
嗯，首先，艾米（Amy）的反应太甜了。

1543
01:10:40.860 --> 01:10:41.440
So sweet.
太甜了。

1544
01:10:41.500 --> 01:10:44.880
She is, I mean, she's waiting for her moment.
她是，我是说，她在等待属于她的时刻。

1545
01:10:45.240 --> 01:10:49.440
Please propose to her somebody because she's like, oh my gosh, this is amazing.
求求谁快向她求婚吧，因为她当时那种表情就像是，天哪，这太棒了。

1546
01:10:49.700 --> 01:10:49.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1547
01:10:49.900 --> 01:10:50.420
Amazing.
太棒了。

1548
01:10:50.720 --> 01:10:51.540
And then you're right.
而且你说得对。

1549
01:10:52.880 --> 01:10:56.820
Jim breaks up with Katie very abruptly.
吉姆非常突然地和凯蒂分手了。

1550
01:10:57.140 --> 01:11:01.640
Jibbity Jenkins actually wrote in and said, Jibbity Jenkins.
Jibbity Jenkins写信来说，Jibbity Jenkins。

1551
01:11:02.640 --> 01:11:04.040
That's not a real name.
那根本不是个真名字。

1552
01:11:04.080 --> 01:11:04.340
Come on.
得了吧。

1553
01:11:04.340 --> 01:11:05.140
First, it's not real.
首先，那不是真名。

1554
01:11:05.320 --> 01:11:06.960
Also, you just rolled into it.
而且，你刚才随口就编出来了。

1555
01:11:07.100 --> 01:11:08.280
Like, I thought it was part of your sentence.
我还以为那是你句子的一部分呢。

1556
01:11:08.420 --> 01:11:10.040
You're like, and then Katie, Jibbity Jenkins.
你当时说的是，然后凯蒂，吉比蒂·詹金斯。

1557
01:11:10.260 --> 01:11:10.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1558
01:11:10.620 --> 01:11:12.880
I was like, is this a poor, a curse word?
我当时还在想，这是什么穷酸词，还是什么脏话吗？

1559
01:11:13.020 --> 01:11:13.520
That's like a Missouri thing, right?
那是密苏里州的说法，对吧？

1560
01:11:13.520 --> 01:11:14.520
I'll be Jibbity Jenkins.
我就叫吉比蒂·詹金斯好了。

1561
01:11:14.700 --> 01:11:15.620
From Dogpatch.
来自狗补丁。

1562
01:11:15.820 --> 01:11:16.520
Jibbity Jenkins.
吉比蒂·詹金斯。

1563
01:11:17.100 --> 01:11:23.780
Jibbity Jenkins says, Jim was kind of a dick to Katie the entire cruise for no reason other
吉比蒂·詹金斯说，吉姆在整个游轮旅行中对凯蒂都很刻薄，原因无他，

1564
01:11:23.780 --> 01:11:25.000
than he wanted to be with Pam.
只是因为他想和帕姆在一起。

1565
01:11:25.260 --> 01:11:27.080
She's really innocent through all this.
在这整件事里，她真的很无辜。

1566
01:11:27.380 --> 01:11:29.860
And then he just breaks up with her.
然后他就直接和她分手了。

1567
01:11:30.080 --> 01:11:32.120
Also, don't break up with someone on a boat.
还有，别在船上和人分手。

1568
01:11:32.700 --> 01:11:33.620
Well, yeah.
嗯，确实。

1569
01:11:33.620 --> 01:11:36.320
A lot of the writers said that, too, to me.
很多编剧也跟我这么说过。

1570
01:11:36.740 --> 01:11:45.880
And I thought it was the most efficient breakup you could possibly have, pretty much.
但我认为这几乎是你所能做出的最高效的分手方式了。

1571
01:11:46.260 --> 01:11:48.020
And we always had time issues.
而且我们总是时间紧迫。

1572
01:11:48.080 --> 01:11:53.900
And I just didn't really want to see a long, drawn-out scene with Katie.
我真的不想看到和凯蒂之间那种冗长拖沓的场景。

1573
01:11:54.200 --> 01:11:55.780
And it just wasn't about that.
而且重点也不在那儿。

1574
01:11:55.780 --> 01:12:00.600
And it seemed to me he was motivated to be brusque and-
在我看来，他当时表现得那么生硬是因为——

1575
01:12:00.600 --> 01:12:00.920
Yeah.
没错。

1576
01:12:01.060 --> 01:12:03.080
He was really upset.
他当时真的很心烦。

1577
01:12:03.080 --> 01:12:03.500
He was hurt.
他受伤了。

1578
01:12:03.500 --> 01:12:05.880
He was hurting, and he just sort of lashed out.
他很痛苦，所以就有点迁怒于人。

1579
01:12:06.080 --> 01:12:07.660
I didn't think it needed to be long.
我觉得没必要拍得那么长。

1580
01:12:07.780 --> 01:12:08.560
I thought it was perfect.
我觉得这样很完美。

1581
01:12:08.720 --> 01:12:13.740
But I also love, and this is something we've talked about a lot, Greg, is that these characters
但我同样喜欢一点，格雷格，这也是我们讨论过很多次的，就是这些角色

1582
01:12:13.740 --> 01:12:14.780
are flawed people.
都是有缺陷的人。

1583
01:12:15.020 --> 01:12:16.140
They're not perfect people.
他们不是完美的人。

1584
01:12:16.380 --> 01:12:19.440
So they're going to have moments like Pam was petty.
所以他们会有一些时刻，比如帕姆当时就很小气。

1585
01:12:19.640 --> 01:12:21.200
I think Pam has been petty.
我觉得帕姆一直都很小气。

1586
01:12:22.520 --> 01:12:28.480
And my character is certainly, we've talked about, my character is certainly not the nicest
而我的角色当然，我们讨论过，我的角色绝对不是最友善的

1587
01:12:28.480 --> 01:12:30.140
person, and-
人，而且——

1588
01:12:30.140 --> 01:12:33.400
You went the longest, being not the nicest of any character.
你可是坚持最久，表现得最不友善的角色了。

1589
01:12:33.640 --> 01:12:33.980
Yes.
没错。

1590
01:12:34.180 --> 01:12:38.240
And which was great, because then when we got into season nine, and I was kind of casting
这很棒，因为当我们进入第九季时，我当时还在琢磨

1591
01:12:38.240 --> 01:12:42.420
about for what the arc of season nine should be, it was like, well, there's only one character
第九季的角色弧线该是什么样，当时就想，好吧，只剩下一个角色

1592
01:12:42.420 --> 01:12:45.080
left who hasn't warmed up at all.
完全没有变得讨喜。

1593
01:12:45.280 --> 01:12:47.840
Let's put Angela through hell this year.
今年就让安吉拉经历地狱般的磨难吧。

1594
01:12:48.500 --> 01:12:51.140
And let her soften just a smidge.
然后让她稍微软化一点。

1595
01:12:51.280 --> 01:12:52.780
Let her deserve a happy ending.
让她配得上一个幸福的结局。

1596
01:12:53.100 --> 01:12:53.320
Yeah.
没错。

1597
01:12:54.520 --> 01:12:59.640
So then we have a scene where we see that Captain Jack and Meredith are sneaking away
所以我们安排了一场戏，看到杰克船长和梅雷迪思偷偷溜走

1598
01:13:01.560 --> 01:13:04.120
to make out, get it on, something.
去亲热、鬼混，或者做点什么。

1599
01:13:04.360 --> 01:13:08.340
Meredith's going to come back later without a shirt on and just a life preserver.
梅雷迪思后来会回来，没穿上衣，只套着一个救生圈。

1600
01:13:08.340 --> 01:13:09.580
The letter her dad wrote her.
她爸爸写给她的那封信。

1601
01:13:09.680 --> 01:13:10.700
Do you remember that letter?
你还记得那封信吗？

1602
01:13:11.000 --> 01:13:11.240
Yeah.
记得。

1603
01:13:11.580 --> 01:13:13.900
That said, dear Kate, stop taking your clothes off.
信上说，亲爱的凯特，别再脱衣服了。

1604
01:13:14.060 --> 01:13:14.620
Thanks, dad.
谢谢你，老爸。

1605
01:13:15.140 --> 01:13:15.620
Yes.
没错。

1606
01:13:16.500 --> 01:13:21.360
Well, this gives Michael the opening to take the microphone and really start his presentation,
好吧，这给了迈克尔一个机会，让他可以拿起麦克风，真正开始他的演讲，

1607
01:13:21.980 --> 01:13:25.120
which he does by announcing that the ship is sinking.
他演讲的内容是宣布船正在下沉。

1608
01:13:25.380 --> 01:13:25.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1609
01:13:26.540 --> 01:13:31.660
Most of the people don't realize that this is a metaphor, passengers panic, and a man jumps
大多数人没意识到这只是个比喻，乘客们陷入了恐慌，还有个人跳了

1610
01:13:31.660 --> 01:13:32.200
overboard.
下去。

1611
01:13:33.400 --> 01:13:38.000
JT wrote in to ask who was the actual person who jumped in the water.
JT写信来问，那个真正跳进水里的人是谁。

1612
01:13:38.340 --> 01:13:41.580
And a lot of people are asking, what happened to that person?
很多人都在问，那个人后来怎么样了？

1613
01:13:42.680 --> 01:13:43.120
Yes.
是啊。

1614
01:13:43.220 --> 01:13:46.940
Well, that was one of the non-Dunder Mifflin people on the boat.
嗯，那是船上非邓德·米夫林公司的乘客之一。

1615
01:13:47.220 --> 01:13:51.520
And as I recall, he was not supposed to jump off the boat.
据我回忆，他本不应该跳船的。

1616
01:13:52.220 --> 01:13:59.360
As I recall, I mean, I may be blowing this because it was a while ago, but I think there
据我回忆，我是说，我可能记错了，因为那是很久以前的事了，但我记得

1617
01:13:59.360 --> 01:14:03.540
was a little bit of shock that one of the extras jumped off the boat in that take.
当时有个群演在那个镜头里跳了船，大家都挺震惊的。

1618
01:14:03.640 --> 01:14:07.860
And I think we were probably not supposed to let him jump off the boat.
而且我觉得我们当时可能不该让他跳船的。

1619
01:14:08.940 --> 01:14:15.680
Well, on the DVD commentary, Greg, you said he really jumped out of the window into the
嗯，在DVD评论音轨里，格雷格，你说他真的从窗户跳进了

1620
01:14:15.680 --> 01:14:16.840
freezing cold water.
冰冷刺骨的水里。

1621
01:14:17.020 --> 01:14:17.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1622
01:14:17.660 --> 01:14:25.900
And you said that you always felt bad that there is no, like, this person jumped into the
你说你一直觉得很内疚，因为没有，比如，这个人跳进了

1623
01:14:25.900 --> 01:14:26.600
It wasn't on camera.
没拍到镜头里。

1624
01:14:26.700 --> 01:14:27.860
It wasn't on camera.
没拍到镜头里。

1625
01:14:28.240 --> 01:14:29.920
He didn't jump in a boat.
他不是从船上跳下去的。

1626
01:14:30.160 --> 01:14:31.340
He didn't jump in a boat.
他不是从船上跳下去的。

1627
01:14:31.340 --> 01:14:33.260
Like, he had to be fished out of the water.
总之，他得被人从水里捞上来。

1628
01:14:33.480 --> 01:14:34.640
It could have been just a rubber dinghy there.
那儿可能只是个橡皮艇。

1629
01:14:35.020 --> 01:14:37.180
I believe it only happened the one time.
我相信那只发生过一次。

1630
01:14:37.360 --> 01:14:38.060
Yeah, I think so.
是啊，我也这么觉得。

1631
01:14:38.180 --> 01:14:44.020
I think he went, I think he may have either misinterpreted some direction or he just was
我觉得他要么是误解了什么指令，要么就是

1632
01:14:44.020 --> 01:14:44.820
super enthusiastic.
太积极了。

1633
01:14:44.820 --> 01:14:49.980
I don't, I have a slight memory of that being a little too gorilla.
我不确定，我隐约记得那有点太拼了。

1634
01:14:51.420 --> 01:14:54.300
That's like Kent was out there running that shot.
当时好像是肯特在外面负责那个镜头。

1635
01:14:55.480 --> 01:14:59.260
Kent was in the boat that was supposed to catch him, but he went and took the shot.
肯特当时在应该接住他的船上，但他跑去拍镜头了。

1636
01:14:59.940 --> 01:15:05.700
Well, I loved at, so this is around 17 minutes, 34 seconds for my time code people, but I love
嗯，我很喜欢，对于看时间码的朋友，这大概在17分34秒左右，但我喜欢

1637
01:15:05.700 --> 01:15:09.980
that the Dunder Mifflin employees know immediately that there's no emergency.
邓德·米夫林的员工立刻就知道根本没有紧急情况。

1638
01:15:10.320 --> 01:15:14.060
And like, even like Kevin and Angela, like we're in a booth together.
就像凯文和安吉拉，我们当时在一个隔间里。

1639
01:15:14.360 --> 01:15:16.280
Oscar, I guess, is off somewhere being snarky.
奥斯卡我猜是在别处冷嘲热讽。

